1152](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:52:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2ab70bf05085f9891fa0512d2754b6e7a2fe3a75","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/2ab70bf05085f9891fa0512d2754b6e7a2fe3a75","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/2ab70bf05085f9891fa0512d2754b6e7a2fe3a75/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32"}]},{"sha":"b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI2NmY4MmYzZTg2YTdjZjI5ZWFjNjIwYzk3ZGQzNWI1MTE1OTFhMzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-29T21:45:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T21:45:05Z"},"message":"feat(interviewer): async submit — persist window, accept fast, synthesize in the scheduler sweep (#667)\n\nFixes #665 (durable track; the immediate on-prem gateway timeout bump is\nalready live on eToro).\n\n## Problem\n`POST /interview/submit` ran 60–90s of inline LLM synthesis on the\nrequest. Intermediate proxies (on-prem nginx default\n`proxy_read_timeout` 60s) 504'd the plugin mid-flight **while the server\ncompleted and committed anyway** — ticks misreported `failed`, buffers\nnever pruned, and the busiest agents' reports appeared \"missing\" (see\nthe corrected diagnosis on #665: webclaw's 63 memories had committed at\n08:01:45 under the install-default agent).\n\n## Design\nDefault path (`interview_async_submit: bool = True`, escape hatch back\nto inline):\n1. Validate exactly as before → **mask** → persist the window as a\ndurable `interview_jobs` doc (doc id = `job_<sha1(node:from:to)>` —\nduplicate submits upsert one job).\n2. **Advance the forward-only watermark and return 200 `accepted`\nimmediately** — the events are durable server-side, so the node may\nsafely prune on this response.\n3. Synthesis runs off-request: a fire-and-forget task per submit\n(strong-ref'd) plus the hourly scheduler sweep\n(`process_pending_interview_jobs`, merged into `run_interview_schedule`)\nas the durable retry path — attempts capped\n(`interview_job_max_attempts=3` → `failed_permanent`), and the\ndeterministic bulk attempt id keeps every retry idempotent.\n\n**Wire-compatible with deployed plugins**: they advance/prune on any 2xx\nwith a numeric watermark and don't gate on `status`. Legacy inline path\npreserved verbatim behind the flag (`run_interview` refactored into mask\n+ `_synthesize_and_write(advance_watermark_after=…)`, byte-identical\nbehavior).\n\n## Tests\n- New `tests/test_interview_async_submit.py` (10 tests):\naccepted+watermark+job-doc, processor→memories→done, idempotent\nre-submit (duplicate_attempt dedup),\nfailure→pending→retry→`failed_permanent` at cap, flag-off legacy\nbehavior, sweep summary.\n- `tests/test_api_interview.py`: 22/22 unchanged (conftest pins\n`INTERVIEW_ASYNC_SUBMIT=false` for legacy tests; the new file opts in\nper-test).\n- Full root suite: 3985 passed; 12 failures verified pre-existing\n(identical with this diff stashed).\n- Ruff clean.\n\n## Review pointers\n- `query_documents` uses `where: {\"status\": \"pending\"}` (same JSONB\npattern as `skills_inbox.py`).\n- Done job docs retain their **masked** events (no cleanup yet — a\nfuture prune could shrink the collection).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8605a163003c186102d02f709c8046fc65102c60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/8605a163003c186102d02f709c8046fc65102c60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqanRhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlLQQADjxZ3G+TH8Ph8veDw+6ET+H\n16REHFNTBZB/m8n+xUqgoJ3m15nIm+rs00o+IZBqb8ANkQHpQoAcIoJoOJZkL4Vh\ni+WrwIymOOcx5pX7Ul9pTNeaGqLRWzaoIoPsHNtmrdXiDmmTNkx18fN+VRPCqOvy\nKjtYGQHD2TLDB55OcVZQqZ03TO8n4meVTX5YEFT6wxW0AgdLTsL81ch0EQNEHt34\nz4X9sMX2PyUIIlKPRl7f5wlUat0q0zVWB29tqMFUxztYtcoTS0hhW1N4D7Q9Fa2B\n6XLhpNTxOxAHdZxQwtUVbPrxj2Feaum3Dv7xxgRekIA0AoargyNkdj71nfQ/nMGz\nQz5xO9RnEIvbOk28gzMitTm18EIf01KPSmbrYDCTZ9uaB+G081B+XaebAm3bzjb7\nlQ0gIKRzspdw726yXdR2OCho5GNLGoWRI3SkGrc82v5gAgEx96PXYkPE0Qj3w0Av\nnXsKvkuXNjkEPIp2VrIEAFzSeeFCxYnPPEd+frE+zw9YGha1MVSYixiRYpAkpO/m\nI+jwoZuvtRfBpGH3SW5pVlOu+Enh7d4XBo/wUZqxKwSNAcgsj+4a1NVW+G/J36/z\nflbZM4xiV/22WWMzw8PLbSovJ3DCyzvi0UfhGWnw58s+oQmkcoXv9OuwNty1wmh/\n7Hc4X5hmIZ91ig2lZfE8\n=7nGD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8605a163003c186102d02f709c8046fc65102c60\nparent 41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1785361505 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785361505 +0300\n\nfeat(interviewer): async submit — persist window, accept fast, synthesize in the scheduler sweep (#667)\n\nFixes #665 (durable track; the immediate on-prem gateway timeout bump is\nalready live on eToro).\n\n## Problem\n`POST /interview/submit` ran 60–90s of inline LLM synthesis on the\nrequest. Intermediate proxies (on-prem nginx default\n`proxy_read_timeout` 60s) 504'd the plugin mid-flight **while the server\ncompleted and committed anyway** — ticks misreported `failed`, buffers\nnever pruned, and the busiest agents' reports appeared \"missing\" (see\nthe corrected diagnosis on #665: webclaw's 63 memories had committed at\n08:01:45 under the install-default agent).\n\n## Design\nDefault path (`interview_async_submit: bool = True`, escape hatch back\nto inline):\n1. Validate exactly as before → **mask** → persist the window as a\ndurable `interview_jobs` doc (doc id = `job_<sha1(node:from:to)>` —\nduplicate submits upsert one job).\n2. **Advance the forward-only watermark and return 200 `accepted`\nimmediately** — the events are durable server-side, so the node may\nsafely prune on this response.\n3. Synthesis runs off-request: a fire-and-forget task per submit\n(strong-ref'd) plus the hourly scheduler sweep\n(`process_pending_interview_jobs`, merged into `run_interview_schedule`)\nas the durable retry path — attempts capped\n(`interview_job_max_attempts=3` → `failed_permanent`), and the\ndeterministic bulk attempt id keeps every retry idempotent.\n\n**Wire-compatible with deployed plugins**: they advance/prune on any 2xx\nwith a numeric watermark and don't gate on `status`. Legacy inline path\npreserved verbatim behind the flag (`run_interview` refactored into mask\n+ `_synthesize_and_write(advance_watermark_after=…)`, byte-identical\nbehavior).\n\n## Tests\n- New `tests/test_interview_async_submit.py` (10 tests):\naccepted+watermark+job-doc, processor→memories→done, idempotent\nre-submit (duplicate_attempt dedup),\nfailure→pending→retry→`failed_permanent` at cap, flag-off legacy\nbehavior, sweep summary.\n- `tests/test_api_interview.py`: 22/22 unchanged (conftest pins\n`INTERVIEW_ASYNC_SUBMIT=false` for legacy tests; the new file opts in\nper-test).\n- Full root suite: 3985 passed; 12 failures verified pre-existing\n(identical with this diff stashed).\n- Ruff clean.\n\n## Review pointers\n- `query_documents` uses `where: {\"status\": \"pending\"}` (same JSONB\npattern as `skills_inbox.py`).\n- Done job docs retain their **masked** events (no cleanup yet — a\nfuture prune could shrink the collection).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:45:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b66f82f3e86a7cf29eac620c97dd35b511591a32/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b"}]},{"sha":"41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQxZjExNTJhNjUyZjgwYTNjMGE0YWM5YjY3NTlmZmI4NjExN2YxOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-29T20:59:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T20:59:22Z"},"message":"fix(core-api): reserved-id guard as a storage-boundary chokepoint + episode-path regression test (#670)\n\n## Context\nOn eToro on-prem, bare-\\`agent_id=\\\"main\\\"\\` (the reserved firehose\nidentity) episode writes were observed landing **despite\n\\`RESERVED_AGENT_ID_POLICY=reject\\`**, suggesting the reserved-id guard\n(#505) was bypassed by the episode-persist path.\n\n## Investigation — no bypass\nTraced **every** persist path at the deployed version: REST\n\\`/memories\\` (incl. the plugin's episode auto-persist,\n\\`context-engine.ts\\` → \\`POST /memories memory_type=episode\\`),\n\\`/ingest\\`, STM, crystallizer, interviewer — **all funnel through\n\\`memory_service.create_memory\\` / \\`create_memories_bulk\\`, both\nguarded.** No unguarded writer exists.\n\nThe 353 bare-\\`main\\` episodes leaked **only during a window when\n\\`reject\\` was transiently unset** (deploy/cutover churn). They\n**stopped the moment stable \\`reject\\` came up** (0 in the following 8h\nwhile the guard fired 350–560×/hr). Reproduced on erni: bare-\\`main\\`\nepisode → **409 under reject**, **201 under warn**;\n\\`main-<install_id>\\` → **201** either way. So the guard already covers\nthe episode path — the defect was reject **durability**, not a code\nbypass (handled separately, on-prem installer).\n\n## This PR — defense-in-depth\nAssert the same guard at **\\`storage_client.create_memory\\` /\n\\`create_memories\\`** — the single boundary **every** memory insert\ncrosses — so no present or future caller can persist a bare-\\`main\\` row\nby reaching storage directly and skipping the service guard.\n- Only exact \\`ALWAYS_RESERVED_AGENT_IDS\\` (\\`{\\\"main\\\"}\\`) reject.\n- De-collapsed \\`main-<install_id>\\` (#507) and named ids pass\nuntouched.\n- Reuses \\`enforce_reserved_write_id\\` (lazy import; no new log path, no\nimport cycle).\n\n## Tests\n- **\\`tests/test_reserved_write_storage_chokepoint.py\\`** (hermetic,\n\\`_post\\` stubbed): bare-\\`main\\` rejected at \\`create_memory\\` +\n\\`create_memories\\` under reject;\n\\`main-<install_id>\\`/named/\\`mcp-agent\\` pass; \\`warn\\` does not block.\n-\n**\\`tests/test_api_memories.py::test_reserved_main_episode_rejected_under_reject\\`**\n(integration): \\`POST /memories memory_type=episode agent_id=\\\"main\\\"\\`\n→ **409** under reject; \\`main-<install_id>\\` episode → **201**. Locks\nthe plugin episode path to the guard so a refactor can't quietly reopen\nit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0754a95cb4f35fb7e4eab1d6c356cddbe7a5c14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0754a95cb4f35fb7e4eab1d6c356cddbe7a5c14e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqammqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ00QAFzM7n14uN09Wrb9b6+Iwu9j\n4hUHtOE540ACEtcgUE5G3x7j/8Gt9nTVBNea50b9PN5+tJMFl8pyTHf9bA/sHjNO\nCj/h/9grRnQSwRqvAbjNwac6of32xk+YcQzNHBzM1qfG+R1lFH3CgQ1m+2q0YkZ8\nOKbwvVQ+WfrtmU6R+opa1CRrEgB2UB7kSeJhcBdFT+abXTIAEfsnXJq+CmZZNuUy\nRXmQPIy6Oq7rLFUXOZDmUZV6nzc5DrUzOofff8XLwuc6lYThCzVp91pRLL4OXryo\niz6cJ2UWDB3E9RBTPXxsyDl8WCajXEsVWSYsF+xwQ5d1LKEYZFzhLJpWHqW+Hvoc\n5I7fD8npgvltxW1Z9TMLF1sTbOxVGVrHJ00d8fc295zHFx2o9bKeVv9b4eizbBl5\nc2EspHU41rEG6X81Ez6uqdZAHUTg941zJ0I31uQw2Vi19BPqSA/wOrTHK7OiKNF/\nd6pEj9QVJ7/XWzSSdEYW/fXjZKTa5aRaEklPqOxt6jWQ5fI/BRxvRKJ05OhFHFfl\nxCmon38XeGe3ogjuCAjt2lqLlXV0ShCjKWVZKSGHABj7A/qNZ9IqO8lgs/qRRFWb\nCPuLn/0k8v7UNtZeTDzz+d+2hV+eR6UN/xBTNqG4CKa5/de71cJvCO9SlaC1mKxy\nb2Ps896DBXFsLRjLN6ny\n=0Zf+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0754a95cb4f35fb7e4eab1d6c356cddbe7a5c14e\nparent 4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1785358762 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785358762 +0300\n\nfix(core-api): reserved-id guard as a storage-boundary chokepoint + episode-path regression test (#670)\n\n## Context\nOn eToro on-prem, bare-\\`agent_id=\\\"main\\\"\\` (the reserved firehose\nidentity) episode writes were observed landing **despite\n\\`RESERVED_AGENT_ID_POLICY=reject\\`**, suggesting the reserved-id guard\n(#505) was bypassed by the episode-persist path.\n\n## Investigation — no bypass\nTraced **every** persist path at the deployed version: REST\n\\`/memories\\` (incl. the plugin's episode auto-persist,\n\\`context-engine.ts\\` → \\`POST /memories memory_type=episode\\`),\n\\`/ingest\\`, STM, crystallizer, interviewer — **all funnel through\n\\`memory_service.create_memory\\` / \\`create_memories_bulk\\`, both\nguarded.** No unguarded writer exists.\n\nThe 353 bare-\\`main\\` episodes leaked **only during a window when\n\\`reject\\` was transiently unset** (deploy/cutover churn). They\n**stopped the moment stable \\`reject\\` came up** (0 in the following 8h\nwhile the guard fired 350–560×/hr). Reproduced on erni: bare-\\`main\\`\nepisode → **409 under reject**, **201 under warn**;\n\\`main-<install_id>\\` → **201** either way. So the guard already covers\nthe episode path — the defect was reject **durability**, not a code\nbypass (handled separately, on-prem installer).\n\n## This PR — defense-in-depth\nAssert the same guard at **\\`storage_client.create_memory\\` /\n\\`create_memories\\`** — the single boundary **every** memory insert\ncrosses — so no present or future caller can persist a bare-\\`main\\` row\nby reaching storage directly and skipping the service guard.\n- Only exact \\`ALWAYS_RESERVED_AGENT_IDS\\` (\\`{\\\"main\\\"}\\`) reject.\n- De-collapsed \\`main-<install_id>\\` (#507) and named ids pass\nuntouched.\n- Reuses \\`enforce_reserved_write_id\\` (lazy import; no new log path, no\nimport cycle).\n\n## Tests\n- **\\`tests/test_reserved_write_storage_chokepoint.py\\`** (hermetic,\n\\`_post\\` stubbed): bare-\\`main\\` rejected at \\`create_memory\\` +\n\\`create_memories\\` under reject;\n\\`main-<install_id>\\`/named/\\`mcp-agent\\` pass; \\`warn\\` does not block.\n-\n**\\`tests/test_api_memories.py::test_reserved_main_episode_rejected_under_reject\\`**\n(integration): \\`POST /memories memory_type=episode agent_id=\\\"main\\\"\\`\n→ **409** under reject; \\`main-<install_id>\\` episode → **201**. Locks\nthe plugin episode path to the guard so a refactor can't quietly reopen\nit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T20:59:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/41f1152a652f80a3c0a4ac9b6759ffb86117f18b/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56"}]},{"sha":"4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDRjYTdiNWI4ZWM4MzMwYWE2N2I4YWFiYTBhOWJlODliZDIwNzhjNTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"arkash20","email":"55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-29T08:30:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T08:30:25Z"},"message":"chore(search): rename sp -> resolved_profile for clarity (#666)\n\n## What\nRename the local variable `sp` → `resolved_profile` in\n`ResolveSearchProfile.execute()`.\n\n`sp` held the validated search profile (agent-level, then merged over\nthe tenant default), and every downstream `.get(\"knob\", CONSTANT)` read\nfrom it. The abbreviation carried no meaning and was easy to confuse\nwith the `search_params` dict built from it. `resolved_profile` makes\nthe in (`search_profile`) → out (`resolved_profile`) → `search_params`\nflow self-documenting.\n\n## Scope\n- Pure rename. **No behaviour change.**\n- ruff check ✅, ruff format ✅ (the longer identifier wrapped two\ndict-literal lines).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9935ca5bae81050fff4b54d07001ad57711f65e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/9935ca5bae81050fff4b54d07001ad57711f65e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqabohCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQskQABBV2748yRSGOA7BPkbsbwWT\n6ouf0+f1zXyQ8ZnYMVfgJGa/7Fzq1rukJtdiiduvQn0TQUZlSj2McJDMVDQWmkZL\nECiDB9ZpaWUV36EMKEdohc9iTI5FAg0T/QIEKXp2eyH4z0Iso6OqOEwpMPpSwQ0U\n1CB6/HJO6vUWGs8g5NnOj9yHIP73m9upSfq85vlBjhenhTmRrlT7/LBAvtfR4E1Q\ndh6bpn3Bvx3cpJttVy7m9eAFi3DmgMVYheJGyBZ2+7zGIEF/us7jo8K0CPJB6pGo\nyfFbu7HH6ZpM7OMo1cn3yXtr4Co7xVIo/j12te2WH29J1iGyVrF75AL4vKf/hJf+\n5l0Lw53fmIDvfdNifJgS/UcPIOa7LKk1MaZEWyOSX64Vf5Jf0HU504Wea9J4DhlV\n4xr2K8U1vI11K99gCTT8vWaA6eZvwrMYvei3CGnRtjwjK/M61HavCp1XH8Rua+Gy\ngpFOJwbqPiSrElyDOiFJHBqdFe5IBydeX9c7u5bhwlnOAauShbSNS7S7ws5hKmNf\nOE0DBRBq1+ZcuCqWJe5e0hqeEsIMmdmTt1FCOEpP4RIKDCrLycZdMB/CJbp/SUSq\neKfJZHFG2N0xuyFZTFhrbX1eGysFlM/0dK2pdB1ulCamuMKg8sltI5OwSAuZ3uwx\n/ci+rJbXs6yhhd5GObrW\n=yTMw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9935ca5bae81050fff4b54d07001ad57711f65e7\nparent 8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443\nauthor arkash20 <55495209+arkash20@users.noreply.github.com> 1785313825 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785313825 +0300\n\nchore(search): rename sp -> resolved_profile for clarity (#666)\n\n## What\nRename the local variable `sp` → `resolved_profile` in\n`ResolveSearchProfile.execute()`.\n\n`sp` held the validated search profile (agent-level, then merged over\nthe tenant default), and every downstream `.get(\"knob\", CONSTANT)` read\nfrom it. The abbreviation carried no meaning and was easy to confuse\nwith the `search_params` dict built from it. `resolved_profile` makes\nthe in (`search_profile`) → out (`resolved_profile`) → `search_params`\nflow self-documenting.\n\n## Scope\n- Pure rename. **No behaviour change.**\n- ruff check ✅, ruff format ✅ (the longer identifier wrapped two\ndict-literal lines).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Arkady Mankovsky <arkash20@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T08:30:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/4ca7b5b8ec8330aa67b8aaba0a9be89bd2078c56/comments","author":{"login":"arkash20","id":55495209,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDk1MjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55495209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20","html_url":"https://github.com/arkash20","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkash20/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443"}]},{"sha":"8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDhhMzVhMWUwZjVlNGIwYTI1ZmVjMTE4YzRmNTBlNzNjNDllOTI0NDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-28T21:27:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T21:27:44Z"},"message":"chore(fleet): bump plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.16.0 (arm #658 task-trail capture) (#664)\n\nBump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION 2.15.2 -> 2.16.0 for onprem-v2.11.12\n(backend-v2.25.0). Plugin 2.16.0 carries #658 (fix for #654): OpenClaw\n`task_runs` are mirrored into the interview buffer, so\ntool/write-pipeline-driven agents (e.g. webclaw) finally produce\nnon-empty interviews — the capture gap we hit in prod. Superset of\n2.15.2 (de-collapse #507 / recall #530 / interviewer #564 preserved).\nTask capture defaults on (`MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_TASKS`) but still gated\nby `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER` + per-tenant `interviewer.enabled`, so the\nfloor bump alone activates nothing. Floor invariant holds\n(MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY 2.6.0 unchanged).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a5073dd100d45ecb6881cd473aa26d4e316f9fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6a5073dd100d45ecb6881cd473aa26d4e316f9fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaR7RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh7kQABvULNUOy7Z1NuWurWvhcFf5\nJx030/LpWv//6b1KSWiov6KOWYSnTOFHEBfO9UP8yz2Xadkfh+RRG6B1d7te4bim\n8spS0PEVMOmsC7GDXMIS/ORmk04xH0Ui7NqX7SiXQmBPYG9IZqHbkAUMYtP4PHtu\n9zQ1r+kzdE8xxPw3BzWLZHw8jJIu4gwLMBsxYYbWPRL5+I5hSRShwm7Df9pWA1w9\nvYeow1L5A/pptaa8QPioE8s/lrNpwDy1icWvVrCV2mCAEpCi9fRjfTgw1Gz3rt0R\nj9CvKDieJCB9pAE9XFSSoHKGbd6ahkE263dI6iIPj4uZOLZJZKRvkPbUGrd3IBSo\nO6Fh0JtMnavbU7aiQ6O3idrdRPCFcvh1JGLtDusabRwkV9DijLrZLzUsjYA++I6r\nuz15Ftz3uSdn2g1dN74GteeBPZRyjF5/YGGK7EDuYBq/BCeinbOgJN0M5TNxWs2Y\nvvaRT4/10ZDBFWfZ2S/u4/QCrMHCSgjBva2W3cDA9dmeEYEEuKPkweyWGAOb0bc7\n1vtjOCT0jv1qFPxsRkQbJ9DIxLmh4BnvfNgHgpB+5Gtx0djRNWK/0tUUhLsFTctj\nU3KAMVi+jV6tbEPL8H4px18Ojj5sgq99L2YqoWDeBrNk2OEVcIgLjWQ2dU8N1uXg\ng7MCHAYj6+63jPQ2l0vh\n=7ncN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6a5073dd100d45ecb6881cd473aa26d4e316f9fd\nparent 8ce3a92727dc8fb5c8bffca15966b81da82d93c1\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1785274064 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785274064 +0300\n\nchore(fleet): bump plugin auto-upgrade floor to 2.16.0 (arm #658 task-trail capture) (#664)\n\nBump MIN_RECOMMENDED_PLUGIN_VERSION 2.15.2 -> 2.16.0 for onprem-v2.11.12\n(backend-v2.25.0). Plugin 2.16.0 carries #658 (fix for #654): OpenClaw\n`task_runs` are mirrored into the interview buffer, so\ntool/write-pipeline-driven agents (e.g. webclaw) finally produce\nnon-empty interviews — the capture gap we hit in prod. Superset of\n2.15.2 (de-collapse #507 / recall #530 / interviewer #564 preserved).\nTask capture defaults on (`MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_TASKS`) but still gated\nby `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER` + per-tenant `interviewer.enabled`, so the\nfloor bump alone activates nothing. Floor invariant holds\n(MIN_AUTO_DEPLOY 2.6.0 unchanged).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T21:27:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73c49e92443","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8a35a1e0f5e4b0a25fec118c4f50e73