## Performance\n\n* **entities:** add HNSW index on entities.name_embedding\n([#660](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/660))\n([f8e8229](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d))\n\n\n### Dependencies\n\n* bump the uv-minor-patch group across 4 directories with 8 updates\n([#649](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/649))\n([79857d4](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f))\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>plugin: 2.16.0</summary>\n\n##\n[2.16.0](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/compare/plugin-v2.15.2...plugin-v2.16.0)\n(2026-07-28)\n\n\n### Features\n\n* **plugin:** interviewer task-trail capture — mirror OpenClaw task_runs\ninto the interview buffer\n([#658](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/issues/658))\n([ba5f4b7](https://github.com/caura-ai/caura-memclaw/commit/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951))\n</details>\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nSigned-off-by: release-please[bot] <release-please[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: caura-deploy-bot[bot] <265395343+caura-deploy-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T21:18:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8ce3a92727dc8fb5c8bffca15966b81da82d93c1","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/8ce3a92727dc8fb5c8bffca15966b81da82d93c1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/8ce3a92727dc8fb5c8bffca15966b81da82d93c1/comments","author":{"login":"caura-deploy-bot[bot]","id":265395343,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOD9Gcjw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229147182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/caura-deploy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caura-deploy-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951"}]},{"sha":"ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGJhNWY0Yjc2YTZhMjYxZjNjODg4NGY2YmNmNjI0YmU3ZTVlYTg5NTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"ran-taig","email":"ran@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-28T21:07:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T21:07:29Z"},"message":"feat(plugin): interviewer task-trail capture — mirror OpenClaw task_runs into the interview buffer (#658)\n\nFixes #654.\n\n## Problem\n\nArmed, highly-active agents produced **empty interviews indefinitely**\n(`\"no new events since cursor\"`). The Phase-1 buffer captures only the\nhost message stream (`context-engine.ingest()`); task/sub-agent-driven\nwork — the dominant mode on the eToro fleet (`oc-webclaw-prod`: 363\nmemories in 3h, zero interviews) — is recorded in OpenClaw's\n**`task_runs` SQLite** and never enters the chat stream. Wrong source,\nnot wrong plumbing: no configuration could fix it.\n\n## Approach\n\n**The buffer stays; a second source feeds it.** The two sources cover\ndisjoint work types (chat-driven agents → existing `ingest()` capture,\nproven correct; task/sub-agent work → this PR). At interview time — no\nbackground poller — the `interview_request` handler mirrors the\ntask-trail **delta** into the same durable buffer, then reads the window\nas before. The buffer's seq/prune/watermark machinery and the frozen\nserver contract (#558) are untouched; the server needs **zero changes**\n(`kind` is free-form ≤64 chars, verified at `routes/interview.py:39`).\n\n**Event mapping — at most two events per task:**\n- first seen → `kind:\"task\"` (`[task <runtime>/<label>] <task>`, session\nfrom `child_session_key`)\n- terminal transition (`ended_at` set — deliberately not a status-enum\ncheck; enums drift across OpenClaw versions) → `kind:\"task_result\"` with\n`terminal_summary`/`error` and `outcome`\n- progress-only bumps emit nothing\n\n## Version tolerance (OpenClaw ≥ 2026.4, verified against openclaw\nsource)\n\n| OpenClaw | task_runs location |\n|---|---|\n| 2026.4–2026.5 | standalone `<base>/tasks/runs.sqlite`\n(`resolveTaskRegistrySqlitePath`) |\n| ≥ 2026.6 | consolidated state DB, **unstable filename** (store\nrefactor; `task-registry.paths.ts` removed) |\n\nSo the DB is **discovered**, not hardcoded (env override → sidecar cache\n→ legacy path → shallow `sqlite_master` scan), and columns are\n**probed** via PRAGMA with graceful degradation to the minimum set.\n`node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync` read-only over WAL — no new dependency\n(OpenClaw ≥2026.4 hosts already run Node ≥22.5, since OpenClaw itself\nuses `DatabaseSync`), and WAL readers never block the gateway's writes.\n\n## Fail-soft + observability (issue remedy #3)\n\nAny failure (DB missing / locked / reshaped / no `node:sqlite`) degrades\nto `{synced: 0, note: \"task-db-unavailable: …\"}`, surfaced as\n`task_trail` + `synced_tasks` in the command result — operators can now\ntell **\"idle\"** from **\"not captured\"**. A tick can never fail on the\ntask DB. Bounded: ≤200 events/tick (sidecar advances only for emitted\nrows → remainder drains next tick); sidecar pruned past OpenClaw's 7-day\ntask retention.\n\nFlags: `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_TASKS` — **default ON** with the interviewer\n(this is the fix for #654, not an optional feature; `\"false\"` is the\nescape hatch). `MEMCLAW_TASK_DB_PATH` — operator override for relocated\nstate.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **11-case task-trail suite**: both layouts (+ decoy non-task DBs),\nold-schema fallback, required-column degradation,\ndelta/no-op/cap/resume, sidecar prune, torn sidecar, already-terminal\ndouble-emit.\n- `interview-command` tests pinned to a tmp base dir so the handler's\npre-read sync can never scan the real `~/.openclaw` of a dev machine.\n- **Full plugin suite: 389/389.**\n- **Real-disk check**: discovery against a genuine OpenClaw install's\nWAL `runs.sqlite` resolves, opens read-only, and syncs cleanly.\n- Node-service-level impact: none on the hot path — sync runs only\ninside the hourly handler, read-only WAL, ms-scale, fail-soft.\n\n## Versioning / rollout\n\nVersion deliberately **left to release-please** (plugin component →\n2.16.0 on merge; package.json/manifest/version.ts are its managed\nfiles). Rollout: plugin floor 2.16.0 on the armed eToro nodes;\nacceptance = the #654 repro inverted (webclaw returns `submitted:true,\nsynced_tasks>0` within 2 ticks; idle agents keep returning \"no new\nevents\" with `synced_tasks:0`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b924a02db86c7258b7836fde610091d59fa6bb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/7b924a02db86c7258b7836fde610091d59fa6bb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaRoRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEMwQACMbMaheuDAL6RO/locUsnwE\nGFlXsKvGONyOBQHb2rTrxaPA0w0sTLGqKiRIv+QRN1F3UiitooyFaz9z2BdRhDCh\nvvYnsC2VBCVbhiydknvZLecx+uxt0mcCeTWCndGnO4UQbex/MMYfTicbx0MXp6N1\ndxFL1aXvIQcKRq54IPyGq1n3eZpo+Hiv9VNIfpjPYqCTFpqMj4XYm8hrHm5Nu3pp\nPwlMtWhukzZ63eEo16fiO2FZHJxdfl8qnIHTh7qCJtuQirF9xIBezQNz53Ucv1ED\nz5eNN+M+s8da+zo+WJwYNP11zjGQqMQM+09BW0u5bLNrbtUjLOwODvn9v7hbBmM9\nabFaOUJ44BWbmu3SBYAzqrrnbn+jGlwgadIhG5XkCi9n71/UXA9Z/rsQg2DezIC8\nRrysJ6qYfSkS7UO+73GE7xjs7guBWTtnSOe/DlcfQRDqfVUgzXOxgqnDRnDQj5+P\nk88Ir765QJVkjPgR9l3iuOnuNy7OgcVaIhgzgMXHhRYWy9mk+jbd3EbRfMx18y56\nxdi3CqSAl+yOhTxFRwa6SQWVxX31RDi1QUjiUfGrnp8VSEFwBuumAfhYexBjq+k9\n/s/Kp6AoWqT91Yg+IuBvKXNv0sWRBCoM0I+4sCh3UF2YfVmpEL01Khkqx1M4Q0lq\nXsaKdMyMu/GZmxQ+SCXM\n=TqFY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7b924a02db86c7258b7836fde610091d59fa6bb4\nparent 550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e\nauthor ran-taig <ran@caura.ai> 1785272849 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785272849 +0300\n\nfeat(plugin): interviewer task-trail capture — mirror OpenClaw task_runs into the interview buffer (#658)\n\nFixes #654.\n\n## Problem\n\nArmed, highly-active agents produced **empty interviews indefinitely**\n(`\"no new events since cursor\"`). The Phase-1 buffer captures only the\nhost message stream (`context-engine.ingest()`); task/sub-agent-driven\nwork — the dominant mode on the eToro fleet (`oc-webclaw-prod`: 363\nmemories in 3h, zero interviews) — is recorded in OpenClaw's\n**`task_runs` SQLite** and never enters the chat stream. Wrong source,\nnot wrong plumbing: no configuration could fix it.\n\n## Approach\n\n**The buffer stays; a second source feeds it.** The two sources cover\ndisjoint work types (chat-driven agents → existing `ingest()` capture,\nproven correct; task/sub-agent work → this PR). At interview time — no\nbackground poller — the `interview_request` handler mirrors the\ntask-trail **delta** into the same durable buffer, then reads the window\nas before. The buffer's seq/prune/watermark machinery and the frozen\nserver contract (#558) are untouched; the server needs **zero changes**\n(`kind` is free-form ≤64 chars, verified at `routes/interview.py:39`).\n\n**Event mapping — at most two events per task:**\n- first seen → `kind:\"task\"` (`[task <runtime>/<label>] <task>`, session\nfrom `child_session_key`)\n- terminal transition (`ended_at` set — deliberately not a status-enum\ncheck; enums drift across OpenClaw versions) → `kind:\"task_result\"` with\n`terminal_summary`/`error` and `outcome`\n- progress-only bumps emit nothing\n\n## Version tolerance (OpenClaw ≥ 2026.4, verified against openclaw\nsource)\n\n| OpenClaw | task_runs location |\n|---|---|\n| 2026.4–2026.5 | standalone `<base>/tasks/runs.sqlite`\n(`resolveTaskRegistrySqlitePath`) |\n| ≥ 2026.6 | consolidated state DB, **unstable filename** (store\nrefactor; `task-registry.paths.ts` removed) |\n\nSo the DB is **discovered**, not hardcoded (env override → sidecar cache\n→ legacy path → shallow `sqlite_master` scan), and columns are\n**probed** via PRAGMA with graceful degradation to the minimum set.\n`node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync` read-only over WAL — no new dependency\n(OpenClaw ≥2026.4 hosts already run Node ≥22.5, since OpenClaw itself\nuses `DatabaseSync`), and WAL readers never block the gateway's writes.\n\n## Fail-soft + observability (issue remedy #3)\n\nAny failure (DB missing / locked / reshaped / no `node:sqlite`) degrades\nto `{synced: 0, note: \"task-db-unavailable: …\"}`, surfaced as\n`task_trail` + `synced_tasks` in the command result — operators can now\ntell **\"idle\"** from **\"not captured\"**. A tick can never fail on the\ntask DB. Bounded: ≤200 events/tick (sidecar advances only for emitted\nrows → remainder drains next tick); sidecar pruned past OpenClaw's 7-day\ntask retention.\n\nFlags: `MEMCLAW_INTERVIEWER_TASKS` — **default ON** with the interviewer\n(this is the fix for #654, not an optional feature; `\"false\"` is the\nescape hatch). `MEMCLAW_TASK_DB_PATH` — operator override for relocated\nstate.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **11-case task-trail suite**: both layouts (+ decoy non-task DBs),\nold-schema fallback, required-column degradation,\ndelta/no-op/cap/resume, sidecar prune, torn sidecar, already-terminal\ndouble-emit.\n- `interview-command` tests pinned to a tmp base dir so the handler's\npre-read sync can never scan the real `~/.openclaw` of a dev machine.\n- **Full plugin suite: 389/389.**\n- **Real-disk check**: discovery against a genuine OpenClaw install's\nWAL `runs.sqlite` resolves, opens read-only, and syncs cleanly.\n- Node-service-level impact: none on the hot path — sync runs only\ninside the hourly handler, read-only WAL, ms-scale, fail-soft.\n\n## Versioning / rollout\n\nVersion deliberately **left to release-please** (plugin component →\n2.16.0 on merge; package.json/manifest/version.ts are its managed\nfiles). Rollout: plugin floor 2.16.0 on the armed eToro nodes;\nacceptance = the #654 repro inverted (webclaw returns `submitted:true,\nsynced_tasks>0` within 2 ticks; idle agents keep returning \"no new\nevents\" with `synced_tasks:0`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Ran Taig <ran@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T21:07:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/ba5f4b76a6a261f3c8884f6bcf624be7e5ea8951/comments","author":{"login":"ran-taig","id":254242316,"node_id":"U_kgDODyduDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254242316?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig","html_url":"https://github.com/ran-taig","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ran-taig/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e"}]},{"sha":"550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU1MGM4ZThlZDQyN2ZiNGFmY2E3MDZkZGY3ZWUwMGM4ZDY0ZDA4OGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-28T14:44:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T14:44:00Z"},"message":"style(serve): keep common/serve.py <=88 cols for the enterprise vendoring gate (#662)\n\n## Why\n\n`common/serve.py` (added in #661) has a 91-col line. OSS CI doesn't\nformat-check `common/`, so it merged clean — but that file is a\nprerequisite for launching the **enterprise** `platform-*` services the\nsame way, which means vendoring it byte-for-byte into\n`caura-memclaw-enterprise` as an `identical`-policy `common/` file.\n\nEnterprise CI runs `ruff format --check common/` with **no resolved\nconfig** → ruff's **88-col default**. A >88-col vendored line fails that\ngate, while the byte-identical drift check simultaneously forbids\nreformatting *only* the enterprise copy. That's the exact wedge from the\n2026-06 `structlog_config` drift incident (fixed by #563). Fixing it\nhere on the OSS source keeps both copies byte-identical **and**\n88-col-clean.\n\n## What\n\n- Reflow the one offending line (`--timeout-keep-alive` arg) to the\n88-col form via `ruff format --isolated` — the width both repos'\n`common/` gates use.\n- Document the ≤88-col vendoring constraint in the module docstring so\nit isn't reintroduced.\n\nNo behaviour change. `tests/test_serve.py` unchanged and green; `ruff\ncheck` clean; still valid at the repo's 110-col config too.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48376372bbc4eb4b715948ab8e6fd3e7c6f6bc38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/48376372bbc4eb4b715948ab8e6fd3e7c6f6bc38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaMAxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOkQQAFhmTDbTpsNfyop308AA4m0b\nkC5pmYQlnddHdGh/r0CJxaoVd8IFnmZoACqxb53kYtcxqs0aECq7QxYjkYVBaxyd\n6LiCfv88q0VHhVcU/pxB69QrrQU/rfO84Dh9JA08vC4TfECXuEp7Yae59DrSZVJq\ngII08fU9hOD4Ed6EvIBeT5x3nTycID1ulcXZ1Gq8vc3j9RjaGRfZ7eVa4hqPKgST\nVeUwFKAk5+Y6bkKeOapKr6MQd+gR722dPd/iw3bBLTokkLfMgCsqHDYA0sDNM94C\n21CHaGOqE/IoCQyyLhXQwxH4NTUW7uMmnl0vqJNrD3+SZSDvdjQFXYGvrvT0LMEC\nWSrxnM+N3CJ/OHl1ykZxzUFSAcQcEXNjl/zrJDYGisBqddsborCFITAwPwTqO1ud\n1vSqv2+smLMOgOf+nX2XG7Cydv6XaZC1w911NQjww6hFk5wNARcptKOquy9TRe67\n2PFHYIjO/TicsSPTawCyCoIRGbdM1RIQXRWeO8gvbE22thoKiReBXXlt2eyQfaGe\nn0hm9tQwpdNsIy+4DRcPzz3cxwnpDM8A7fUMQfH9gm7M/5UjwBddQatipND3cKe+\nM2GQilV1dca8hlErCMHL4JqDqWkGu/Qmpogjq1iUwI705voMkjl1AtaOCSRChey0\njKzGwNO7L0j8f9d3fPHK\n=Jjq/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 48376372bbc4eb4b715948ab8e6fd3e7c6f6bc38\nparent b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785249840 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785249840 +0300\n\nstyle(serve): keep common/serve.py <=88 cols for the enterprise vendoring gate (#662)\n\n## Why\n\n`common/serve.py` (added in #661) has a 91-col line. OSS CI doesn't\nformat-check `common/`, so it merged clean — but that file is a\nprerequisite for launching the **enterprise** `platform-*` services the\nsame way, which means vendoring it byte-for-byte into\n`caura-memclaw-enterprise` as an `identical`-policy `common/` file.\n\nEnterprise CI runs `ruff format --check common/` with **no resolved\nconfig** → ruff's **88-col default**. A >88-col vendored line fails that\ngate, while the byte-identical drift check simultaneously forbids\nreformatting *only* the enterprise copy. That's the exact wedge from the\n2026-06 `structlog_config` drift incident (fixed by #563). Fixing it\nhere on the OSS source keeps both copies byte-identical **and**\n88-col-clean.\n\n## What\n\n- Reflow the one offending line (`--timeout-keep-alive` arg) to the\n88-col form via `ruff format --isolated` — the width both repos'\n`common/` gates use.\n- Document the ≤88-col vendoring constraint in the module docstring so\nit isn't reintroduced.\n\nNo behaviour change. `tests/test_serve.py` unchanged and green; `ruff\ncheck` clean; still valid at the repo's 110-col config too.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T14:44:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/550c8e8ed427fb4afca706ddf7ee00c8d64d088e/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850"}]},{"sha":"b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI2MWZjYjU5MzZhNDgxMmQ2YmYxMDQ4YjYxYWI4NWY2NmIyNjk4NTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-28T13:30:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T13:30:00Z"},"message":"fix(logging): route uvicorn parent-supervisor lines through structlog (#661)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a `common/serve.py` launcher and points the **core-api** and\n**core-storage-api** Docker `CMD`s at it (`python -m common.serve <app>\n--settings <module:attr> ...`), so the uvicorn multiprocess **parent\nsupervisor** configures structlog before starting.\n\n## Why\n\nWith `uvicorn --workers 2`, the parent supervisor never imports the ASGI\napp module, so the import-time `configure_logging()` in\n`<service>/app.py` runs **only in the workers**. The parent's own\nlifecycle lines — emitted via the `uvicorn.error` logger — bypass the\nstructlog JSON pipeline and reach Datadog with no `status` field, where\nthey're mis-classified as `status:error`:\n\n```\nINFO:     Started parent process [8]\nINFO:     Waiting for child process [22]\nINFO:     Received SIGTERM, exiting.\nINFO:     Uvicorn running on http://0.0.0.0:8000 ...\n```\n\nThis was the **single biggest source of false `status:error`** across\nthe Cloud Run services in the 2026-07 error sweeps. It's functionally\nharmless, but it pollutes `status:error` queries and log monitors (the\nalert added after the embedding incident keys off message content, not\n`status`, so nothing is broken — this is log-hygiene).\n\n## How\n\n- `common/serve.py`: calls `configure_logging(...)` from the **service's\nown settings object** (identical args to `app.py`), then\n`uvicorn.run(..., log_config=None)`.\n- `log_config=None` is the key: uvicorn then installs **no** handlers of\nits own, so `uvicorn.{error,access}` keep `propagate=True` and reach the\nstructlog root handler in **both** the parent and the workers. The\nparent's lifecycle lines emit as JSON with `status:info`. (Letting\nuvicorn apply its default `LOGGING_CONFIG` would re-plain-text them.)\n- Reuses the existing `configure_logging()` /\n`_route_third_party_to_root()` machinery — no new formatter.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_serve.py`: the launcher reads settings and calls\n`configure_logging` from those fields + `uvicorn.run(log_config=None)`\n(no server started).\n- `tests/test_logging.py`: an INFO record on the `uvicorn.error` logger\nrenders as `severity:INFO` / `status:info` through the pipeline.\n\n## Verification gate ⚠️\n\nThe **end-to-end** parent-supervisor output can only be confirmed with a\nrunning multi-worker server. **Please verify in staging before merge** —\n`env:staging` is off in Datadog, so check via `gcloud logging read` on\nthe staging revisions that the supervisor lines (`Started parent\nprocess`, `Received SIGTERM`) now emit as JSON with `status:info` and\nthat nothing else regressed. This touches the shared logging path for\nboth services, so the staging check is the real gate.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe enterprise **platform-\\*** services share this same pattern; they'll\nbe wired in a follow-up once this `common/` change vendors over.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fbb991cec20cea99369131bc5287a3a29b94b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0fbb991cec20cea99369131bc5287a3a29b94b30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaK7YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjoEQAKASRHScQpNASUrKS5p1u5NQ\nCv3jhfhrshfjHs2Tm6GY/UXLz2e/I4L3R8ZZLfirhHxQ0vd8r3GOuWzGt33bGzqo\nSR7s5lyvyIwarUX0sUoiml/qhrFP0rgRtEa00MDbY8qG/swgUZvqVSc/RAfhxAnQ\nlvY9pdn22IPGqZYmXCvnjwPVckKvztMhPh4BDThVr1CRUQ4AVFwTJqhRhlSXqdWf\nEm1Iye1jnlNfXSCP6tVyGSUsqmxSlZPAtSfrm5zswe13QkO8+UzK++gpe3JBNrHf\nC8E98HVTujhvulcTcJI16JSH2+WBss1MieEZGtc8SmP8YTqBaAJ5rn45FF+WTvkB\n6r1mtD98mSJ77iKTmIsJAj0Vy3C8F6F2VB/06QLm8dBC8SKtYM2RDazr1vC8klFI\nNkgO6tUm7nKBgFgwvVH7i1bTlM5nDVodZNmPLTHR/9B2mE4znLoHaV58Pyk1Y7+7\nQ1ItYbWbGGLSjNnTINrgaqaNj2RzPJODkQJhJxD2ukyx+mNT9Yz2eUkTmyKgrXoJ\nq0GTo4C2wIkimku3fI2bEaLZpv1JI3N43wsx6MSnfjDR1DM/LfVrxhJ1StbGdv+T\nOY/BGFq6scejNwoTvwSdSEozF1vmVikMQ2ATqrthbFQ6CRVpuCI09crh94vENWZl\nNb7NclJLOQMBbbLOQR34\n=w2Ko\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0fbb991cec20cea99369131bc5287a3a29b94b30\nparent f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785245400 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785245400 +0300\n\nfix(logging): route uvicorn parent-supervisor lines through structlog (#661)\n\n## What\n\nAdds a `common/serve.py` launcher and points the **core-api** and\n**core-storage-api** Docker `CMD`s at it (`python -m common.serve <app>\n--settings <module:attr> ...`), so the uvicorn multiprocess **parent\nsupervisor** configures structlog before starting.\n\n## Why\n\nWith `uvicorn --workers 2`, the parent supervisor never imports the ASGI\napp module, so the import-time `configure_logging()` in\n`<service>/app.py` runs **only in the workers**. The parent's own\nlifecycle lines — emitted via the `uvicorn.error` logger — bypass the\nstructlog JSON pipeline and reach Datadog with no `status` field, where\nthey're mis-classified as `status:error`:\n\n```\nINFO:     Started parent process [8]\nINFO:     Waiting for child process [22]\nINFO:     Received SIGTERM, exiting.\nINFO:     Uvicorn running on http://0.0.0.0:8000 ...\n```\n\nThis was the **single biggest source of false `status:error`** across\nthe Cloud Run services in the 2026-07 error sweeps. It's functionally\nharmless, but it pollutes `status:error` queries and log monitors (the\nalert added after the embedding incident keys off message content, not\n`status`, so nothing is broken — this is log-hygiene).\n\n## How\n\n- `common/serve.py`: calls `configure_logging(...)` from the **service's\nown settings object** (identical args to `app.py`), then\n`uvicorn.run(..., log_config=None)`.\n- `log_config=None` is the key: uvicorn then installs **no** handlers of\nits own, so `uvicorn.{error,access}` keep `propagate=True` and reach the\nstructlog root handler in **both** the parent and the workers. The\nparent's lifecycle lines emit as JSON with `status:info`. (Letting\nuvicorn apply its default `LOGGING_CONFIG` would re-plain-text them.)\n- Reuses the existing `configure_logging()` /\n`_route_third_party_to_root()` machinery — no new formatter.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_serve.py`: the launcher reads settings and calls\n`configure_logging` from those fields + `uvicorn.run(log_config=None)`\n(no server started).\n- `tests/test_logging.py`: an INFO record on the `uvicorn.error` logger\nrenders as `severity:INFO` / `status:info` through the pipeline.\n\n## Verification gate ⚠️\n\nThe **end-to-end** parent-supervisor output can only be confirmed with a\nrunning multi-worker server. **Please verify in staging before merge** —\n`env:staging` is off in Datadog, so check via `gcloud logging read` on\nthe staging revisions that the supervisor lines (`Started parent\nprocess`, `Received SIGTERM`) now emit as JSON with `status:info` and\nthat nothing else regressed. This touches the shared logging path for\nboth services, so the staging check is the real gate.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe enterprise **platform-\\*** services share this same pattern; they'll\nbe wired in a follow-up once this `common/` change vendors over.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T13:30:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b61fcb5936a4812d6bf1048b61ab85f66b269850/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d"}]},{"sha":"f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY4ZTgyMjlkZjM5MGQ5NTMzMjczMmE0MThkMjZmYTE0N2U1NGI1N2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-28T12:29:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T12:29:46Z"},"message":"perf(entities): add HNSW index on entities.name_embedding (#660)\n\n## What\n\nAdds an HNSW index on `entities.name_embedding` (migration `033`),\nmirroring `ix_memories_embedding_hnsw` from `001`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe entity cross-link discovery path —\n`PostgresService.entity_discover_cross_links` → `POST\n/api/v1/storage/entities/discover-cross-links` — runs a per-candidate\nANN search over a tenant's entities:\n\n```sql\nJOIN LATERAL (\n    SELECT ... FROM entities e\n    WHERE e.tenant_id = :tenant_id AND e.name_embedding IS NOT NULL ...\n    ORDER BY e.name_embedding <=> m.embedding\n    LIMIT 10\n) e ON true\n```\n\n`entities.name_embedding` has had **no ANN index since `001`**\n(migration `012` notes this explicitly). Without one, every candidate\nmemory triggers a full sequential scan of the tenant's entities —\n`O(candidates × entities)` cosine computations in a single request. On\nlarge tenants this exceeds the caller's 120 s timeout, observed as a\n**`504 Gateway Timeout`** on the storage endpoint in prod + staging\n(2026-07). The index makes each lookup `O(log n)` and speeds up entity\nlinking generally.\n\n## How\n\n- `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS\nix_entities_name_embedding_hnsw ON entities USING hnsw (name_embedding\nvector_cosine_ops) WITH (m = 16, ef_construction = 64)`.\n- Built `CONCURRENTLY` inside `op.get_context().autocommit_block()` so\nit doesn't take an AccessExclusiveLock on `entities` during the build —\nsame idiom as `012`/`024`. `IF NOT EXISTS` keeps it idempotent on the\nadvisory-lock-serialised startup migration path.\n- Params (`m`, `ef_construction`) and opclass (`vector_cosine_ops`)\nmatch the memories index.\n\n## Notes / risk\n\n- **No behaviour change** — results are identical; only the query plan\nchanges. No test changes needed; CI validates the migration applies.\n- The filtered-ANN-by-`tenant_id` characteristic is the same as the\nexisting `memories.embedding` recall path (single-column HNSW + a\n`tenant_id` filter), so no new failure mode is introduced.\n- One-time cost: the `CONCURRENTLY` build runs once in the startup\nmigration on first deploy; on a large `entities` table it adds a\none-time build to that replica's startup (other replicas wait on the\nadvisory lock). Acceptable and non-locking.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbba104820672bdc6ca0560c2b70c73a1979c0ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/fbba104820672bdc6ca0560c2b70c73a1979c0ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaKC6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbU0QAK8LuPf03pNt02hkOaIlBWpM\n7nSplyKspvnblLhIP20r5xD7I1jB8n9O6cGvOlyRmeatiTm4KluvItYl6+Xru4AP\n1YbttRBR0CWM+LGhe0LOK6kh7ucDc1B5kJpn0BlEDzZhTrXvuvsvLqGJyEKGQqCZ\n/Ms699wUB7jdyTk8HYEDw0xrw+HBeyh+6vuQHrj9csS+nEAEsfa27z5Ia9XyYTVn\nCxG++YvCwS8tBcHcvoG2c7jT0FvBic2aFYvufQ3lXewIIL823TOrj4oJA9do+IsG\ngHj7Buv5mhkSCJTst0MH9qCnlPYW+DpTtxg9bd6EHLhKo89QoF6aW/NpWXqtwbRU\n4CXkux+5wPm1PElJIZnBYDuf2vPbHSjbtQS4MRicvPfYNqVsHF5QCO2IANZg9tSQ\nU/AB10H53YKpPMXIaTYgPNwHRMA3E2NXnuaW+BJWL6OWJxFMFWh9EDPFBA9zsso+\n87Wu357aERv3IALH6s3VAoKYXSWWL/W9GRZA1JeLW4mOBvi3DuPU7Djhv1+to74Y\nnWMPXR1RZuUm15wMb8WVk7H/RLdxwKxad4EqaRXo7uuvxJwo/+d5iYFEIjp/fqur\nZIaQeGGOMhKF4656YfXeIHIDbkFQG+ueyOA26i8k1CLASsS+BCoae8QsfQmkJFRU\n+7LO4vWIsIWLLH/5fWv2\n=Gqm+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fbba104820672bdc6ca0560c2b70c73a1979c0ed\nparent 59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785241786 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785241786 +0300\n\nperf(entities): add HNSW index on entities.name_embedding (#660)\n\n## What\n\nAdds an HNSW index on `entities.name_embedding` (migration `033`),\nmirroring `ix_memories_embedding_hnsw` from `001`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe entity cross-link discovery path —\n`PostgresService.entity_discover_cross_links` → `POST\n/api/v1/storage/entities/discover-cross-links` — runs a per-candidate\nANN search over a tenant's entities:\n\n```sql\nJOIN LATERAL (\n    SELECT ... FROM entities e\n    WHERE e.tenant_id = :tenant_id AND e.name_embedding IS NOT NULL ...\n    ORDER BY e.name_embedding <=> m.embedding\n    LIMIT 10\n) e ON true\n```\n\n`entities.name_embedding` has had **no ANN index since `001`**\n(migration `012` notes this explicitly). Without one, every candidate\nmemory triggers a full sequential scan of the tenant's entities —\n`O(candidates × entities)` cosine computations in a single request. On\nlarge tenants this exceeds the caller's 120 s timeout, observed as a\n**`504 Gateway Timeout`** on the storage endpoint in prod + staging\n(2026-07). The index makes each lookup `O(log n)` and speeds up entity\nlinking generally.\n\n## How\n\n- `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS\nix_entities_name_embedding_hnsw ON entities USING hnsw (name_embedding\nvector_cosine_ops) WITH (m = 16, ef_construction = 64)`.\n- Built `CONCURRENTLY` inside `op.get_context().autocommit_block()` so\nit doesn't take an AccessExclusiveLock on `entities` during the build —\nsame idiom as `012`/`024`. `IF NOT EXISTS` keeps it idempotent on the\nadvisory-lock-serialised startup migration path.\n- Params (`m`, `ef_construction`) and opclass (`vector_cosine_ops`)\nmatch the memories index.\n\n## Notes / risk\n\n- **No behaviour change** — results are identical; only the query plan\nchanges. No test changes needed; CI validates the migration applies.\n- The filtered-ANN-by-`tenant_id` characteristic is the same as the\nexisting `memories.embedding` recall path (single-column HNSW + a\n`tenant_id` filter), so no new failure mode is introduced.\n- One-time cost: the `CONCURRENTLY` build runs once in the startup\nmigration on first deploy; on a large `entities` table it adds a\none-time build to that replica's startup (other replicas wait on the\nadvisory lock). Acceptable and non-locking.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T12:29:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8e8229df390d95332732a418d26fa147e54b57d/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068"}]},{"sha":"59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDU5MTE1Y2UzMTljMDcwNmFkNzM0OTE1NzJjOTg2ZTcyNmFmNTgwNjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-27T21:48:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T21:48:42Z"},"message":"ci: sync dependabot-automerge edge-case handling with #933 (#657)\n\nSyncs the two edge-case tweaks from enterprise #933's review into this\ncopy, so all three `dependabot-automerge.yml` workflows (enterprise /\ncaura-ops / OSS) stay logic-identical:\n- **bail-fast on `ERROR`:** a StatusContext in `error` state (lowercase,\nupper-cased to `ERROR`) now bails immediately instead of polling the\nfull 20-min deadline.\n- **drop bare `409` from the head-moved grep:** `branch was modified`\nalready matches GitHub's real `--match-head-commit` mismatch message;\ndropping `409` avoids a false-match swallowing a genuine error (failing\nvisible on ambiguity is safer for a merge gate).\n\nBoth are no-op for this repo's actual required checks (CheckRuns), pure\nconsistency + robustness. No change to the merge gate itself.\n\n(caura-ops #245 gets the same sync in its parallel PR.)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"793e22d590a5744bcafdf1124924ae8ff6caa331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/793e22d590a5744bcafdf1124924ae8ff6caa331"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ9I6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQuAQAFbhSIDqtbTMwH7y/ZJFNlDU\nX5YMkIB9ObXH+6KJiBLwE/y3lK5mf4qiYdyC9pHs0HgraLeg0+s7iNPFUoikQNyO\n2/wQZOHrmdRqsKnCZAOb/ehebzEt6BUxl5T8mQ4QLqWQaKRZMsu+BO9bIqoJxBLK\nNLvQwZAhZhzkMnZw/wKO+8mgk09FJ5fJ5/aomT92yh/hlvLdJ3A3dxhrVIyC8tgw\nHxrbiL6EKTtvK4zv1EGod3nEbZz9tAKuFudwJLj1KkXfedvJqu1iXtaNTjNKRy5l\nY41r5vhj4s1Y8+5+e7fdB0luHNLt/Jg6LmPuYi+/Q0KX+Sto5AqrDNVi/bN0RGI9\nx79T6rQ9ZltdaRgs0mP/JH3fNQQRTlskcrVq+OzALO8sBApnlrKt2dah3IY+U75F\nyO+AxUTnbCZFZ3sac9Q2b+YJcgg7Ll5XIEk0Qcuj0jSG3Fc4JKi+67KqVdXFqCbG\nwGr+aiX5J9Mp4CdRqWQMsWve9xvEEINj+OkuQlVdwrdMnnxCTZxOfP2VZicmitHx\n/8EN7mE8KFgzAQ7iyJi9zqcVKD6ATc37faEbi5pmfpmn2WP4LHXrrOiqbja2xRVQ\nDlfqr4gv5cb3qwVYbYga8rIY1uUAAycQLnNBjldTqgdv5R+iIH6J+jgseqYq1y20\nyt3CkpOpu3uUQwKeNESN\n=TrhI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 793e22d590a5744bcafdf1124924ae8ff6caa331\nparent 370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785188922 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785188922 +0300\n\nci: sync dependabot-automerge edge-case handling with #933 (#657)\n\nSyncs the two edge-case tweaks from enterprise #933's review into this\ncopy, so all three `dependabot-automerge.yml` workflows (enterprise /\ncaura-ops / OSS) stay logic-identical:\n- **bail-fast on `ERROR`:** a StatusContext in `error` state (lowercase,\nupper-cased to `ERROR`) now bails immediately instead of polling the\nfull 20-min deadline.\n- **drop bare `409` from the head-moved grep:** `branch was modified`\nalready matches GitHub's real `--match-head-commit` mismatch message;\ndropping `409` avoids a false-match swallowing a genuine error (failing\nvisible on ambiguity is safer for a merge gate).\n\nBoth are no-op for this repo's actual required checks (CheckRuns), pure\nconsistency + robustness. No change to the merge gate itself.\n\n(caura-ops #245 gets the same sync in its parallel PR.)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T21:48:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/59115ce319c0706ad73491572c986e726af58068/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed"}]},{"sha":"370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDM3MGI4ODQxMzhhMGVjOTk0MzlmN2ZiZGU5MTY5YzY2Yjc0MmVmZWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-27T21:12:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T21:12:46Z"},"message":"ci: add Dependabot minor/patch auto-merge workflow (OSS-tailored) (#656)\n\n## What\nPorts enterprise's `dependabot-automerge.yml` (incl. the enterprise-#929\n`-R \"$REPO\"` fix) so Dependabot's **`pip-`/`uv-`/`npm-minor-patch`**\nGROUP PRs self-merge once required CI is green — draining the ~12-PR\nmanual backlog.\n\nTailored for this repo's model:\n- **Groups:** pip/uv/npm-minor-patch (this repo's group names).\n- **Required checks:** `CI` + `dco`, read from *classic branch\nprotection* (this repo uses branch protection, not a ruleset).\n- **Defensive merge:** if the merge is blocked it logs and exits 0\n(no-op) instead of failing — so it's **safe to merge before the bypass\nbelow is set up**.\n\nScope mirrors the enterprise carve-out: only those minor/patch groups\nauto-merge; majors, constraint-updates, and the github-actions group\nstay manual. Merge runs under the DEPLOY_APP token, gated by the script\n(not `--auto`) and pinned via `--match-head-commit`.\n\n## ⚠️ Prerequisite before it actually merges\n`main` requires **1 approving review**, and there is currently **no App\nbypass** configured for it (no ruleset bypass actor / no\n`bypass_pull_request_allowances`). So an App-token merge is rejected on\n\"review required\" until you add the deploy App to **Settings → Branches\n→ main → Allow specified actors to bypass required pull requests**. (The\n`DEPLOY_APP` org secrets are already shared with this repo via\nrelease-please.)\n\nThis is a **public-repo** auto-merge, so it also means Dependabot\nminor/patch groups would merge without the 1 human approval — flagging\nthat explicitly since it's your call.\n\nVerified: `CI` + `dco` both pass on this repo's Dependabot PRs (so the\ngate is satisfiable), and this pairs with #655 which unblocks the client\nCI lint.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"f4d969ca771588a0e8d1a2125fb876526fd16c4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f4d969ca771588a0e8d1a2125fb876526fd16c4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ8nOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACUsQACY/3PohwhxyPS3vaxS+Gc6q\nFWwzEZE1eEMny4IWXS2Lev5SDbmiMYgzqkLSdvXEbhKi87O4EoYGVCiQcBc9AoOx\nYHetrUVC1aVbs4+Ic9AnDAiRgASdoMtaNy1EAdiC9W0mpt+p2cDMLSueM166k4Tp\n/VlBBNuijn7ia8YdNSgXsXpqpA6lpcgB4eevV7/ZHCZ1Qnk9Pmd0h7M/Cf2K8Qcx\nJ37Bf1fBG4SxX8vVuwvTSMo2NfK+9Y/cv8paeVCJXXK57ntfOE3R5i15V/5SE89q\nr56hex2mT+CTZwOj3RrjRv5dOCFb5OZgB6Vr2hGHaN1cShzVNDTUC1+sifQjCjAx\nDkHf56Ag42yBHPbMGDjXfFkuiSUbbLvlm1Ll75ENK0WXK3WBc1DAxCSFbTjvRCpa\nPdNaBPieUVEvC6wJd7dd+u3AfXjpCKqa4IMMKRi7c7ujKF+9IHoIkAdkLLrYx0Zv\nZAXIno6nPIPa7MdDvSZQjsJkCMGTaOdsfA66PqhE5RVBiZZyVwgIueYsEO3qpqFT\nuAkbSj1tr1HbhTnkhg5saHY5TuU7ZaznYLtcph9/DBnnbKUDInyJ6hwJw0eAHSZw\nP4xoTLve03ithQ1cXnEt8bmPBMpUY9U8C8fnIkzzAK6xjfDF4lClxGQj4V+ZKtgD\naKdAcOVhL11VSzQAzgYI\n=u+mS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f4d969ca771588a0e8d1a2125fb876526fd16c4d\nparent 24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785186766 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785186766 +0300\n\nci: add Dependabot minor/patch auto-merge workflow (OSS-tailored) (#656)\n\n## What\nPorts enterprise's `dependabot-automerge.yml` (incl. the enterprise-#929\n`-R \"$REPO\"` fix) so Dependabot's **`pip-`/`uv-`/`npm-minor-patch`**\nGROUP PRs self-merge once required CI is green — draining the ~12-PR\nmanual backlog.\n\nTailored for this repo's model:\n- **Groups:** pip/uv/npm-minor-patch (this repo's group names).\n- **Required checks:** `CI` + `dco`, read from *classic branch\nprotection* (this repo uses branch protection, not a ruleset).\n- **Defensive merge:** if the merge is blocked it logs and exits 0\n(no-op) instead of failing — so it's **safe to merge before the bypass\nbelow is set up**.\n\nScope mirrors the enterprise carve-out: only those minor/patch groups\nauto-merge; majors, constraint-updates, and the github-actions group\nstay manual. Merge runs under the DEPLOY_APP token, gated by the script\n(not `--auto`) and pinned via `--match-head-commit`.\n\n## ⚠️ Prerequisite before it actually merges\n`main` requires **1 approving review**, and there is currently **no App\nbypass** configured for it (no ruleset bypass actor / no\n`bypass_pull_request_allowances`). So an App-token merge is rejected on\n\"review required\" until you add the deploy App to **Settings → Branches\n→ main → Allow specified actors to bypass required pull requests**. (The\n`DEPLOY_APP` org secrets are already shared with this repo via\nrelease-please.)\n\nThis is a **public-repo** auto-merge, so it also means Dependabot\nminor/patch groups would merge without the 1 human approval — flagging\nthat explicitly since it's your call.\n\nVerified: `CI` + `dco` both pass on this repo's Dependabot PRs (so the\ngate is satisfiable), and this pairs with #655 which unblocks the client\nCI lint.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T21:12:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/370b884138a0ec99439f7fbde9169c66b742efed/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259"}]},{"sha":"24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDI0YTEzN2FkNjMwODA2YWRlNTA0MzI0ZWQ0N2IzN2Q3NTk3MGYyNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-27T20:27:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T20:27:21Z"},"message":"fix(client-ci): pin ruff to the 0.15 line so client CI stops floating into 0.16 (#655)\n\n## What\nPins the `memclaw_client` dev extra to `ruff>=0.15.4,<0.16` (from\n`ruff>=0.6`).\n\n## Why\n`client-python-ci.yml` installs ruff via `pip install -e \".[dev]\"`. With\n`ruff>=0.6` it floated to **0.16**, whose new default rules fire on\nexisting code — **18 findings** (RUF022 `__all__`-not-sorted, C408, …).\nThat silently red-lined the *Lint (ruff)* step on every `clients/python`\nPR, including the Dependabot `setup-python` bump #640 (which has nothing\nto do with ruff). Note the pre-commit ruff hook is scoped to\n`core-api`/`core-storage-api`, so it never covered the client package.\n\n## Fix\nPin to the **0.15 line**, matching `.pre-commit-config.yaml`'s `rev:\nv0.15.4`. Verified locally:\n- ruff **0.15.4** → `All checks passed!`\n- ruff **0.16.0** → `Found 18 errors`\n\nAdopting ruff 0.16 for the client (fixing the 18 findings) is a\ndeliberate follow-up — same reasoning as the enterprise frozen-lint work\n— not a silent CI-breaking float. This unblocks #640 and other client\nPRs.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"5a357327f5cd517f4eb56d19f6c58fe9d59a6dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/5a357327f5cd517f4eb56d19f6c58fe9d59a6dac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ78pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAihEQAF6VmdFhwnsLE99v4lw01473\n/c5L09EvRm1F3/AZ8ScABaff4iOmT+RKGJs9VwsPlVeTphjsDpF9h6KVQBOV+ZYn\nGuKYQjPfeeUkEpIqLViXFWMWE5zGXasItH0zb/NNCxUQ0jT7VD26p5R3l2hf5sbh\nzVnNBa7oZuDo7UxcqpgDwdkWu0f8ELRJq0ECQkx2/H6D2qv72qLFDVyxAAvOcxhp\nd1k4l5QkK9QsZM9xrPnM0R2KJLZxICEPBmXRhy2iDckckyJg9gLlYQN788lL3fW3\nNdLqTVFogt2RCYN94kIKCQJ+d0Yq4YAI0eeMrENKQqeoSLtrtM8szs2r8fZOUjeU\nSLyfnNLB9470bUG3XJUUdAHk5lBaI2q2eS8AiSfmewMjizkkfiT+VWjN2FXONga7\nIOESUcM0y4NLGoo/CTocQeDueIqmTffZaKsagyrPybQFDBoqP4XHHSc/tb3z7kNL\npKyBCDzjMGk5GZg3ExL4oaq3tqyOXUjnZK35tSCcwZEuf7s+K9/wX1iVmRy+pvSt\n4tTeNDy1R6KpfKqtu27bYl4Ob7yI+WZOHcbAvTsV0RsVGYuPTSXeV6Cb+31PyrGs\nyW7uMonVZqo93j0VDWTSYvES4+4ml5UseePeoSnHOWYFj9YZ+573arFK62wy+HAI\nWgJsIrwhKEBxdcEhb+am\n=MJQ2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5a357327f5cd517f4eb56d19f6c58fe9d59a6dac\nparent b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785184041 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785184041 +0300\n\nfix(client-ci): pin ruff to the 0.15 line so client CI stops floating into 0.16 (#655)\n\n## What\nPins the `memclaw_client` dev extra to `ruff>=0.15.4,<0.16` (from\n`ruff>=0.6`).\n\n## Why\n`client-python-ci.yml` installs ruff via `pip install -e \".[dev]\"`. With\n`ruff>=0.6` it floated to **0.16**, whose new default rules fire on\nexisting code — **18 findings** (RUF022 `__all__`-not-sorted, C408, …).\nThat silently red-lined the *Lint (ruff)* step on every `clients/python`\nPR, including the Dependabot `setup-python` bump #640 (which has nothing\nto do with ruff). Note the pre-commit ruff hook is scoped to\n`core-api`/`core-storage-api`, so it never covered the client package.\n\n## Fix\nPin to the **0.15 line**, matching `.pre-commit-config.yaml`'s `rev:\nv0.15.4`. Verified locally:\n- ruff **0.15.4** → `All checks passed!`\n- ruff **0.16.0** → `Found 18 errors`\n\nAdopting ruff 0.16 for the client (fixing the 18 findings) is a\ndeliberate follow-up — same reasoning as the enterprise frozen-lint work\n— not a silent CI-breaking float. This unblocks #640 and other client\nPRs.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T20:27:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/24a137ad630806ade504324ed47b37d75970f259/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53"}]},{"sha":"b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI0ODljOGY0NDYwMmM3ODM5YzViNGM0ZDdlNGExYmUzYzVkMWJhNTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-27T12:02:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T12:02:17Z"},"message":"fix(embedding): make batch-failure re-embed fallback durable (#653)\n\n## Why\n\nCloses the tail of the **2026-07-27 incident**. #652 capped concurrency\nso the backend stops being thrashed — but it did **not** remove the\nrequest-count amplification, nor the permanence.\n\nA failed 50-item bulk re-embed batch fanned out to **50 in-process tasks\n× 3 re-embed retries × 2 embedding attempts ≈ 300 provider calls**, all\ncontending for the same already-saturated backend. When they exhausted,\nthe rows stayed `embedding=NULL` **with no further recovery** — a manual\nCLI backfill was the only way out. That is exactly how **~430 memories\nwere stranded**: stored, HTTP 200, but not semantically recallable.\n\nI originally claimed #652's gate subsumed this. It doesn't — the gate\nremoves *connection* amplification only. This PR is the actual fix.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe five batch-failure fallbacks now go through the **existing**\n`_schedule_embed_or_reembed` router instead of calling `_reembed_memory`\ndirectly:\n\n| mode | behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| **deferred** (prod) | one cheap `EMBED_REQUESTED` publish per item →\nretry lives on **Pub/Sub with redelivery + DLQ**, and survives instance\nrestart |\n| **inline** (OSS, no worker fleet) | unchanged: in-process retry |\n\nThis makes the permanently-unembedded class **structurally impossible**\nrather than merely less likely.\n\n`is_failure_fallback` is threaded through the router so the **inline**\nbranch keeps its thundering-herd backoff (the provider just failed for\nthe whole batch); the deferred branch ignores it because Pub/Sub owns\nbackoff.\n\n**No new mechanism** — this reuses the same router the hot-path offload\nalready uses, which is why the diff is small. The deliberate comment\nthat previously documented the in-process behaviour is updated to\nexplain the durability rationale.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` clean; module compiles; all 5 sites\nrouted, 0 direct calls remain.\n- 3 new tests in `tests/test_durable_reembed_fallback.py`: deferred\npublishes and does **not** retry in-process; inline retries in-process\n**and** receives the backoff flag; the hot-path default does **not**\ninherit the backoff.\n- ⚠️ **The new tests were not run locally** — `memory_service` pulls in\nthe full app dependency graph that isn't installed in my sandbox\n(`cachetools`, `croniter`, …). CI runs them in the real environment.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7d6c377522b378adb01c6b7cd00163db2f8a4af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/f7d6c377522b378adb01c6b7cd00163db2f8a4af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ0jJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2JQQAGvtbTQ3ClUKnXxWmCfXblxh\naouoOWYZtvQd2diZ+0sAWP2jbkCONyxnLGsnIAxoMTRcR5YpePXZ8xAeX08e+utb\nbVNN6jacOj8Xu+sjB7/sDMzCUakQGedcrZy5pdEF95RH3OpLVavTLQVYO6lKXaEn\nUK0vMAabSP6gbcGTeP6rN2KvVVCG7/y85Y1MR62NKpjBPzGaUoUplk8MzziZgV0e\nE07j9tXPyDAjv+g3Fq59w/+n+Dsf6VxEGQre0SXljB+M5xYkKaUAIzya8xwVls2g\nc+Vy6DiJvjXw02us0lc/QvXnWj+6PH6g0xgKcugoY1qQNSCnx6AxVzFQxmpfOv8N\naYKJnxAcSNg43VYUbNO+UNL1ZB24fc4sDPrM2fEwDqwozEOe3Yd6Bv55acj7d5hb\nf8AXIt5NPgctJTIjv2PmFEFGTakgEFOQ8MZPjUnHe+ZS1MDtn/di5GH5XFWoqDpe\nZNDaARws3OaIZR+KSiYMxySndkDgCDQ8gFjQGqu82rNTar6S6yAEe3jrZrl/VhfT\nC59wbvOsjGPUViBXPI1z0GxOiE8c51liPAAfmIXg1Yu6VcOspSiO8hpx4+JeFv76\nFle04f5yecYPgZ8EadjXOoo8ljgI3Uz2vF1HsENNqifJvahf5oncnuOaNqXtXzjn\n9ajlrDW72pyTJG8EJPti\n=bBbC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f7d6c377522b378adb01c6b7cd00163db2f8a4af\nparent 0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785153737 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785153737 +0300\n\nfix(embedding): make batch-failure re-embed fallback durable (#653)\n\n## Why\n\nCloses the tail of the **2026-07-27 incident**. #652 capped concurrency\nso the backend stops being thrashed — but it did **not** remove the\nrequest-count amplification, nor the permanence.\n\nA failed 50-item bulk re-embed batch fanned out to **50 in-process tasks\n× 3 re-embed retries × 2 embedding attempts ≈ 300 provider calls**, all\ncontending for the same already-saturated backend. When they exhausted,\nthe rows stayed `embedding=NULL` **with no further recovery** — a manual\nCLI backfill was the only way out. That is exactly how **~430 memories\nwere stranded**: stored, HTTP 200, but not semantically recallable.\n\nI originally claimed #652's gate subsumed this. It doesn't — the gate\nremoves *connection* amplification only. This PR is the actual fix.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe five batch-failure fallbacks now go through the **existing**\n`_schedule_embed_or_reembed` router instead of calling `_reembed_memory`\ndirectly:\n\n| mode | behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| **deferred** (prod) | one cheap `EMBED_REQUESTED` publish per item →\nretry lives on **Pub/Sub with redelivery + DLQ**, and survives instance\nrestart |\n| **inline** (OSS, no worker fleet) | unchanged: in-process retry |\n\nThis makes the permanently-unembedded class **structurally impossible**\nrather than merely less likely.\n\n`is_failure_fallback` is threaded through the router so the **inline**\nbranch keeps its thundering-herd backoff (the provider just failed for\nthe whole batch); the deferred branch ignores it because Pub/Sub owns\nbackoff.\n\n**No new mechanism** — this reuses the same router the hot-path offload\nalready uses, which is why the diff is small. The deliberate comment\nthat previously documented the in-process behaviour is updated to\nexplain the durability rationale.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` clean; module compiles; all 5 sites\nrouted, 0 direct calls remain.\n- 3 new tests in `tests/test_durable_reembed_fallback.py`: deferred\npublishes and does **not** retry in-process; inline retries in-process\n**and** receives the backoff flag; the hot-path default does **not**\ninherit the backoff.\n- ⚠️ **The new tests were not run locally** — `memory_service` pulls in\nthe full app dependency graph that isn't installed in my sandbox\n(`cachetools`, `croniter`, …). CI runs them in the real environment.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T12:02:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b489c8f44602c7839c5b4c4d7e4a1be3c5d1ba53/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df"}]},{"sha":"0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDBjNzY0YmJlMmNjNjZjNWQ0NGU1MjU4MGM4ZDMxMWJjNWI1NjQ0ZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-27T11:29:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T11:29:12Z"},"message":"fix(embedding): cap in-flight embed calls to stop pool-exhaustion cascade (#652)\n\n## Incident\n\n**2026-07-27 07:26–09:10Z.** ~77% of embeds failed for ~1h45m; **~430\nmemories were left permanently unembedded** — stored fine, all HTTP\n200s, but not semantically recallable. Silent data-quality loss.\n\n## Root cause: oversubscription of our OWN backend, not a provider\noutage\n\nProd points `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL` at a **self-hosted TEI service**\n(`BAAI/bge-m3`, L4 GPU), not OpenAI:\n\n| side | capacity |\n|---|---|\n| TEI backend | `maxScale 2` × `containerConcurrency 10` = **20\nconcurrent** |\n| core-api demand | `minScale 10` (max 200) instances ×\n**200-connection** pool = **≥2,000** |\n\nWhen bulk volume spiked ~18× (181/hr → 3,274/hr), TEI's 20 slots\nsaturated. Callers queued at the HTTP pool and died on\n`httpx.PoolTimeout` → `openai.APITimeoutError` — **while TEI itself\nstayed healthy, reporting 3.5 ms inference throughout.**\n\nThe self-sustaining part: a failed 50-item batch falls back to 50\nper-item calls, re-jamming the same 20 slots → more failures → more\nfallback.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`EMBEDDING_MAX_CONCURRENCY`** (default 16) caps in-flight provider\ncalls per process — surplus work waits on a cheap semaphore instead of\nholding a connection until the pool times out. Applied at both provider\nchokepoints, acquired **per attempt** so a backing-off retry never\nsquats on a slot.\n- **`EMBEDDING_GATE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`** (default 5.0) bounds the wait.\nDeliberately **below** the tightest caller cap (the search path's 10 s)\n— at or above it the outer timer always fires first and the gate could\nnever attribute the failure to backpressure. On timeout the caller\ndegrades down the *pre-existing* provider-failure path.\n- **Gate logs saturation and timeout distinctly.** During the incident\nthe backend reported 3.5 ms while callers timed out and nothing said\nwhere the time went.\n- **`EMBEDDING_HTTPX_MAX_CONNECTIONS` / `_KEEPALIVE`** split the\nembedding pool from the LLM pool. Both previously read\n`OPENAI_HTTPX_MAX_CONNECTIONS`, so shrinking the embedding pool to match\na small self-hosted backend would also throttle every LLM call — making\nthe one knob you need during an embedding incident unusable.\n- **`read_float_env` promoted to `common/env_utils`** (beside\n`read_int_env`, which that module exists to share);\n`common/llm/constants` delegates to it. The new gate timeout would\notherwise have used a bare `float(os.environ.get(...))` that raises at\nmodule import on a bad value.\n\n## Honest limits of this PR\n\n**This reduces thrash amplitude; it does not restore a capacity\ninvariant.** The cap is *per process*, so 16 × instance count is still\nwell above TEI's capacity. Called out in the constant's comment rather\nthan papered over.\n\n**Two structural follow-ups I deliberately did not fold in** (both\nsurfaced by review, both deserve their own focused change):\n\n1. **The request-count amplifier survives.** The gate removes\n*connection* amplification, but one failed 50-item batch still spawns 50\n× 3 re-embed retries × 2 attempts ≈ 300 gated acquisitions against 16\nslots. Most time out → row stays NULL → same terminal outcome as the\nincident, with no automatic recovery (backfill is a manual CLI). The\nright fix is one function away: swap the in-process\n`track_task(_reembed_memory(..., is_failure_fallback=True))` fallbacks\nfor a durable `EMBED_REQUESTED` publish, whose consumer already has\nPub/Sub redelivery + DLQ + per-tenant slots. That would make the\npermanently-unembedded class structurally impossible — but it changes\nretry semantics and contradicts a deliberate existing comment, so it\nneeds its own review.\n2. **The gate is a single unkeyed global**, while the constraint is\nper-backend. The registry supports simultaneous distinct backends, so a\nsaturated TEI tenant currently throttles an OpenAI tenant. Keying the\ngate on the same backend identity the provider cache already uses is the\ndeeper form.\n\n## Related (already live, not in this PR)\n\nTEI `maxScale` raised **2 → 3** (20 → 30 concurrent). Capped there by\nGPU quota — `NvidiaL4GpuAllocNoZonalRedundancy` allows 3; a quota\nincrease is needed to go further.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 4 new tests in `tests/test_embedding_concurrency_gate.py`: cap\nenforced (30 callers → 3 in-flight), slot released on exception, blocked\nwaiter degrades instead of hanging, gate rebinds per event loop.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` clean on changed files (the 3 remaining\n`G201`/`RUF100` hits are pre-existing on `main`, verified by linting the\npristine tree).\n- Defensive parsing verified: a misconfigured\n`EMBEDDING_GATE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30s` warns and falls back instead of\ncrashing import.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c44dab057e1a47376ed0604f481539d0df80cb6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/c44dab057e1a47376ed0604f481539d0df80cb6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ0EICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6f0QAGxqEEbYLdsbZFWUOuCw8Yg9\nfrSyxXl1I/VHt/DuenCPkQPsj4ij4z4tXW7SP5fKUa8n1TSw8sopNEJDOLEpvBpm\n8bKL2OBZWML58SaLJxTA907i9YQicElBQLyBFXRp7gS8fc1J4T48rve7KPiR8wP+\n5dmT5ny4MWES8LOES2Zy+1KhqTQbAO5V0Qz/GEmVt2Zr2PnZOP+Owv2QuklWbb0h\nNlw4za8MseCUPFQ0vExvTcV7iDumj0IaRpy8wyU8QlLdoYQ+D6AtdEZbgHCbOL4G\n86MV9VSLfRAIj1Dli3swTl0a5u8CrqpYJHc2BLcWf4gHuONe1fsU3aeBoyP0fjNH\niyLxzZ0UOkK+gssXKTHawEmoC903TgUGSUej5oeF9z6IfnktIdLTF76uUJkyn4kk\n1h05zyW2LFjOOIvmRB5Xi6QhPhKiB3e1r9MS/5gmMqyl1kfiHJysY6il0r6tatyW\n0L4KZuHaaW8ZK/HD9P/VcfAkTEts9eaaDantxQLPAy5GdsEavOkqM3HqelhFdX8F\nd7cJ+6jsJMfXizVL4EzzY5dVbPduitM2eFBQ66wxK+2De2yxZVBPBIAjIYdyNWkx\nb6+pOe4JSRVLr1EhQM3Y72zNaUWuYMyh1Zn6NhB48pVJGxVY7N1ZuAoAgv5Y26MP\nnqh2mOEXfhSmW2AQzW/5\n=pedZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c44dab057e1a47376ed0604f481539d0df80cb6a\nparent 79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785151752 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785151752 +0300\n\nfix(embedding): cap in-flight embed calls to stop pool-exhaustion cascade (#652)\n\n## Incident\n\n**2026-07-27 07:26–09:10Z.** ~77% of embeds failed for ~1h45m; **~430\nmemories were left permanently unembedded** — stored fine, all HTTP\n200s, but not semantically recallable. Silent data-quality loss.\n\n## Root cause: oversubscription of our OWN backend, not a provider\noutage\n\nProd points `OPENAI_EMBEDDING_BASE_URL` at a **self-hosted TEI service**\n(`BAAI/bge-m3`, L4 GPU), not OpenAI:\n\n| side | capacity |\n|---|---|\n| TEI backend | `maxScale 2` × `containerConcurrency 10` = **20\nconcurrent** |\n| core-api demand | `minScale 10` (max 200) instances ×\n**200-connection** pool = **≥2,000** |\n\nWhen bulk volume spiked ~18× (181/hr → 3,274/hr), TEI's 20 slots\nsaturated. Callers queued at the HTTP pool and died on\n`httpx.PoolTimeout` → `openai.APITimeoutError` — **while TEI itself\nstayed healthy, reporting 3.5 ms inference throughout.**\n\nThe self-sustaining part: a failed 50-item batch falls back to 50\nper-item calls, re-jamming the same 20 slots → more failures → more\nfallback.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`EMBEDDING_MAX_CONCURRENCY`** (default 16) caps in-flight provider\ncalls per process — surplus work waits on a cheap semaphore instead of\nholding a connection until the pool times out. Applied at both provider\nchokepoints, acquired **per attempt** so a backing-off retry never\nsquats on a slot.\n- **`EMBEDDING_GATE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`** (default 5.0) bounds the wait.\nDeliberately **below** the tightest caller cap (the search path's 10 s)\n— at or above it the outer timer always fires first and the gate could\nnever attribute the failure to backpressure. On timeout the caller\ndegrades down the *pre-existing* provider-failure path.\n- **Gate logs saturation and timeout distinctly.** During the incident\nthe backend reported 3.5 ms while callers timed out and nothing said\nwhere the time went.\n- **`EMBEDDING_HTTPX_MAX_CONNECTIONS` / `_KEEPALIVE`** split the\nembedding pool from the LLM pool. Both previously read\n`OPENAI_HTTPX_MAX_CONNECTIONS`, so shrinking the embedding pool to match\na small self-hosted backend would also throttle every LLM call — making\nthe one knob you need during an embedding incident unusable.\n- **`read_float_env` promoted to `common/env_utils`** (beside\n`read_int_env`, which that module exists to share);\n`common/llm/constants` delegates to it. The new gate timeout would\notherwise have used a bare `float(os.environ.get(...))` that raises at\nmodule import on a bad value.\n\n## Honest limits of this PR\n\n**This reduces thrash amplitude; it does not restore a capacity\ninvariant.** The cap is *per process*, so 16 × instance count is still\nwell above TEI's capacity. Called out in the constant's comment rather\nthan papered over.\n\n**Two structural follow-ups I deliberately did not fold in** (both\nsurfaced by review, both deserve their own focused change):\n\n1. **The request-count amplifier survives.** The gate removes\n*connection* amplification, but one failed 50-item batch still spawns 50\n× 3 re-embed retries × 2 attempts ≈ 300 gated acquisitions against 16\nslots. Most time out → row stays NULL → same terminal outcome as the\nincident, with no automatic recovery (backfill is a manual CLI). The\nright fix is one function away: swap the in-process\n`track_task(_reembed_memory(..., is_failure_fallback=True))` fallbacks\nfor a durable `EMBED_REQUESTED` publish, whose consumer already has\nPub/Sub redelivery + DLQ + per-tenant slots. That would make the\npermanently-unembedded class structurally impossible — but it changes\nretry semantics and contradicts a deliberate existing comment, so it\nneeds its own review.\n2. **The gate is a single unkeyed global**, while the constraint is\nper-backend. The registry supports simultaneous distinct backends, so a\nsaturated TEI tenant currently throttles an OpenAI tenant. Keying the\ngate on the same backend identity the provider cache already uses is the\ndeeper form.\n\n## Related (already live, not in this PR)\n\nTEI `maxScale` raised **2 → 3** (20 → 30 concurrent). Capped there by\nGPU quota — `NvidiaL4GpuAllocNoZonalRedundancy` allows 3; a quota\nincrease is needed to go further.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 4 new tests in `tests/test_embedding_concurrency_gate.py`: cap\nenforced (30 callers → 3 in-flight), slot released on exception, blocked\nwaiter degrades instead of hanging, gate rebinds per event loop.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format` clean on changed files (the 3 remaining\n`G201`/`RUF100` hits are pre-existing on `main`, verified by linting the\npristine tree).\n- Defensive parsing verified: a misconfigured\n`EMBEDDING_GATE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30s` warns and falls back instead of\ncrashing import.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T11:29:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0c764bbe2cc66c5d44e52580c8d311bc5b5644df/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f"}]},{"sha":"79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDc5ODU3ZDQ2MmQ1ZWExNGMxODFkYjMzYzIyYmRiZGVhYzQ3NzYxM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-27T10:03:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T10:03:12Z"},"message":"deps: bump the uv-minor-patch group across 4 directories with 8 updates (#649)\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 7 updates in the /core-api\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.139.2` | `0.140.0`\n|\n| [greenlet](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet) | `3.5.3` |\n`3.5.4` |\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.161.0` | `1.162.0` |\n| [google-genai](https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai) | `2.12.1`\n| `2.14.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.46.0` |\n`2.48.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.4` | `7.1.6` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.15.22` | `0.16.0` |\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 3 updates in the /core-operations\ndirectory: [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi),\n[cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) and\n[ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 4 updates in the /core-storage-api\ndirectory: [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi),\n[greenlet](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet),\n[openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) and\n[ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 6 updates in the /core-worker\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.139.2` | `0.140.0`\n|\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.161.0` | `1.162.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.46.0` |\n`2.48.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.4` | `7.1.6` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.15.22` | `0.16.0` |\n|\n[sentence-transformers](https://github.com/huggingface/sentence-transformers)\n| `5.6.0` | `5.6.1` |\n\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.139.2 to 0.140.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.140.0</h2>\n<h3>Refactors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16049\">#16049</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix links in docs. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15967\">#15967</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add Library Skills documentation. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16041\">#16041</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Update docs to use uv projects by default. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16032\">#16032</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Restructure FastAPI People and related pages. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16015\">#16015</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>👷 Add CI memory benchmark. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16046\">#16046</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👥 Update FastAPI People - Sponsors. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16027\">#16027</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔥 Remove now-obsolete scripts to generate data for FastAPI People.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16016\">#16016</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/255b912928904e3ba5980425a54d6837c8bd1a1c\"><code>255b912</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16050\">#16050</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/892eacd27dcdcfe6c5ea114543ff473cbbfd7c6f\"><code>892eacd</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/027082950068d6e3897b5422ab6cde3168f7d8b0\"><code>0270829</code></a>\n⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16049\">#16049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/ae031be7b5a2df589f63f4d25389cf07b7b8fc86\"><code>ae031be</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f3644b33cdaf1b14868d77f1c309e0a455c6bac8\"><code>f3644b3</code></a>\n📝 Fix links in docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15967\">#15967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1e24ca0e12e9a66cecb1e42780b9116374e2618d\"><code>1e24ca0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/513c396322664bcb3bdcb3946c440a8ed8ef080b\"><code>513c396</code></a>\n👷 Add CI memory benchmark (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16046\">#16046</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/a64dfbbd21a445288ff583d58e1f646fe6baf3af\"><code>a64dfbb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/4f155486f0c1465c5e1f8701544acc10cb8a78bb\"><code>4f15548</code></a>\n📝 Add Library Skills documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16041\">#16041</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/704fbe1439341994100622853f515a8af7ccc2eb\"><code>704fbe1</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.139.2...0.140.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `greenlet` from 3.5.3 to 3.5.4\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/blob/master/CHANGES.rst\">greenlet's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>3.5.4 (2026-07-22)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a crash (segfault) on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14 and\nlater when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet that was\nstarted from a non-empty C-stack-reference state is active.\nSee <code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a potential use-after-free on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14\nand later when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet is\nsuspended holding a <code>_PyCStackRef</code> (for example, mid\nattribute\nresolution). See\n<code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a deadlock on free-threaded builds when a greenlet switch\nhappened\nwhile a <code>PyCriticalSection</code> was held -- for example inside\nasyncio's\n<code>Task.__step</code>, which holds one on the running task for the\nduration of\nthe step. See <code>PR 519\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/pull/519/&gt;</code>.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. note::\nBinary 3.15 wheels are now built with Python 3.15b4. These may not\nbe compatible with earlier or later versions of 3.15. Binary\n3.15 wheels of greenlet from previous releases (e.g., 3.5.3)\nmay not be compatible with Python 3.15b4.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/384be8821a934fbb835e369dda2b9b72107e80be\"><code>384be88</code></a>\nPreparing release 3.5.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/bbdf57b8cccc572639103005bc7dee41d1c309a2\"><code>bbdf57b</code></a>\nAdd note to CHANGES about versions of 3.15 binary wheels may/not be\ncompatibl...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/759902381a85e2ebca2102fab50ffb99b2227a2b\"><code>7599023</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/517\">#517</a>\nfrom ddorian/issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/73a0a1aadf8d45db71754954d588d433fa826a2a\"><code>73a0a1a</code></a>\nFix the suspended C-stack-ref GC test to catch its regression</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/1ff35f431f768e854db323ae14274044a06d9d12\"><code>1ff35f4</code></a>\nMerge branch 'master' into issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/847fb824f6c0590d87963c38c4b2f452a0980b37\"><code>847fb82</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/520\">#520</a>\nfrom dynapx/fix-test-extension-npd</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/0b471ba66bed12fcf7bef969f26705a30a29a5b4\"><code>0b471ba</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/519\">#519</a>\nfrom ddorian/freethread-switch-critical-section</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/d55914df27b30af452e63eb2be41fc9b3ec2c982\"><code>d55914d</code></a>\nSimplify the CHANGES.rst entry</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/78932dc67b6571a920751339cfd88056144e8116\"><code>78932dc</code></a>\nChange notes are for end users, they don't need to go into technical\ndetail</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/39bf70c2cb8c8996ce26bc20e4161fd94c05d380\"><code>39bf70c</code></a>\nHold the C-stack ref snapshot in a std::vector&lt;OwnedObject&gt;</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/compare/3.5.3...3.5.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-cloud-aiplatform` from 1.161.0 to 1.162.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/releases\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.162.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.161.0...v1.162.0\">1.162.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add detailed agent tool definitions for display (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/762079f098e21fff5f914b760671ff2cc1647567\">762079f</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1beta1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Delegate agent resolution to server via geminiAgentConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ab757c7d86f10d38438f9dda50daaa3521b46b29\">ab757c7</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add warning on vertexai.Client instantiation and\nrecommend agentplatform.Client (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f141415043dc9c3d3cdb5850263869b1d6974f3f\">f141415</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - multi-turn user simulation for Gemini Agents\nAPI run_inference (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c74e996d09e7633e7bd66a06df24ecff9224846b\">c74e996</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the correct enum for RagFile.file_status (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/23145f30843febc29cc607930df02b1e083ce39a\">23145f3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add example usage to RAG docstrings (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df3dcd976330f0de50537569d76d9aef1337ed74\">df3dcd9</a>)</li>\n<li>Update product name from &quot;Vertex AI&quot; to &quot;Gemini\nEnterprise Agent Platform&quot; in README, and add a note to rename\nAgent Engine to Agent Runtime in upcoming major release (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a3179c2c7f0480b0d9abe3e205edd7e402ad5f2b\">a3179c2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.161.0...v1.162.0\">1.162.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add detailed agent tool definitions for display (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/762079f098e21fff5f914b760671ff2cc1647567\">762079f</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1beta1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Delegate agent resolution to server via geminiAgentConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ab757c7d86f10d38438f9dda50daaa3521b46b29\">ab757c7</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add warning on vertexai.Client instantiation and\nrecommend agentplatform.Client (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f141415043dc9c3d3cdb5850263869b1d6974f3f\">f141415</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - multi-turn user simulation for Gemini Agents\nAPI run_inference (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c74e996d09e7633e7bd66a06df24ecff9224846b\">c74e996</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the correct enum for RagFile.file_status (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/23145f30843febc29cc607930df02b1e083ce39a\">23145f3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add example usage to RAG docstrings (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df3dcd976330f0de50537569d76d9aef1337ed74\">df3dcd9</a>)</li>\n<li>Update product name from &quot;Vertex AI&quot; to &quot;Gemini\nEnterprise Agent Platform&quot; in README, and add a note to rename\nAgent Engine to Agent Runtime in upcoming major release (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a3179c2c7f0480b0d9abe3e205edd7e402ad5f2b\">a3179c2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/922fa6ae798d3d753426ef2572aaf3574c0a4066\"><code>922fa6a</code></a>\nchore(main): release 1.162.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/issues/7003\">#7003</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\"><code>4331d55</code></a>\nCopybara import of the project:</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/06a9089fc5ca2c53656bd05028814f5c4e06b11c\"><code>06a9089</code></a>\nchore: Handle interactions_data_source as a valid data source</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ab757c7d86f10d38438f9dda50daaa3521b46b29\"><code>ab757c7</code></a>\nfeat: Delegate agent resolution to server via geminiAgentConfig</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/762079f098e21fff5f914b760671ff2cc1647567\"><code>762079f</code></a>\nfeat: Add detailed agent tool definitions for display</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f141415043dc9c3d3cdb5850263869b1d6974f3f\"><code>f141415</code></a>\nfeat: GenAI client - Add warning on vertexai.Client instantiation and\nrecomme...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/23145f30843febc29cc607930df02b1e083ce39a\"><code>23145f3</code></a>\nfix: Use the correct enum for RagFile.file_status</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df3dcd976330f0de50537569d76d9aef1337ed74\"><code>df3dcd9</code></a>\ndocs: GenAI client - Add example usage to RAG docstrings</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/62bc783b94763bb1e49c0f33b5b9ebcee1d3aa55\"><code>62bc783</code></a>\nchore: Add a2a framework test to agentplatform.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a3179c2c7f0480b0d9abe3e205edd7e402ad5f2b\"><code>a3179c2</code></a>\ndocs: Update product name from &quot;Vertex AI&quot; to &quot;Gemini\nEnterprise Agent Platfo...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.161.0...v1.162.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-genai` from 2.12.1 to 2.14.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/releases\">google-genai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.14.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.13.0...v2.14.0\">2.14.0</a>\n(2026-07-22)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config and\nPart.audio_transcription. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dc3d78dc228709c0968554694a884f9fe17a36bc\">dc3d78d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add deprecation warnings to Imagen generate_images, edit_images,\ngenerate_videos (if using prompt/text/image args),\nLiveConnectConfig.GenerationConfig which will be removed in the next\nmajor version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49059181ea0452e160ec61135c29f9c177f19160\">4905918</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.13.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/097a99e6c79f752af1ad055b6daffa384f6d6bc3\">097a99e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.13.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.1...v2.13.0\">2.13.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A new field <code>custom_vocabulary</code> is added to to Live API\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/4eeb1ade8dedb9ccdabe00892d4ff2119b54a444\">4eeb1ad</a>)</li>\n<li>Add model selector (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/bf3dba460092d2f3af7a2b29abe2f0778ff8334d\">bf3dba4</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interaction-api:</strong> Add queued status to interaction\nproto (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/87f1650e169a35cae45e415ad9b9c48e3e53f143\">87f1650</a>)</li>\n<li>Make ASR fields public in v1main and Interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/5b52faaca37744c6a79b2bb37b3204229c445121\">5b52faa</a>)</li>\n<li>Support mTLS in custom client using google auth\nmtls.get_default_ssl_context (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7270e6d5c2854731e953fce04488fcf46bbb4c60\">7270e6d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.11.0 and 2.12.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dddd7c6a2e7b3f3eabcda4417ebb5fa1a0207526\">dddd7c6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-genai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.13.0...v2.14.0\">2.14.0</a>\n(2026-07-22)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config and\nPart.audio_transcription. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dc3d78dc228709c0968554694a884f9fe17a36bc\">dc3d78d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add deprecation warnings to Imagen generate_images, edit_images,\ngenerate_videos (if using prompt/text/image args),\nLiveConnectConfig.GenerationConfig which will be removed in the next\nmajor version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49059181ea0452e160ec61135c29f9c177f19160\">4905918</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.13.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/097a99e6c79f752af1ad055b6daffa384f6d6bc3\">097a99e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.1...v2.13.0\">2.13.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A new field <code>custom_vocabulary</code> is added to message\n<code>.google.cloud.aiplatform.v1beta1.BidiGenerateContentSetup</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/4eeb1ade8dedb9ccdabe00892d4ff2119b54a444\">4eeb1ad</a>)</li>\n<li>Add model selector (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/bf3dba460092d2f3af7a2b29abe2f0778ff8334d\">bf3dba4</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interaction-api:</strong> Add queued status to interaction\nproto (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/87f1650e169a35cae45e415ad9b9c48e3e53f143\">87f1650</a>)</li>\n<li>Make ASR fields public in v1main and Interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/5b52faaca37744c6a79b2bb37b3204229c445121\">5b52faa</a>)</li>\n<li>Support mTLS in custom client using google auth\nmtls.get_default_ssl_context (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7270e6d5c2854731e953fce04488fcf46bbb4c60\">7270e6d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.11.0 and 2.12.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dddd7c6a2e7b3f3eabcda4417ebb5fa1a0207526\">dddd7c6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7c1f70d4103deed1b210a2c3cfe3b155defd672e\"><code>7c1f70d</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.14.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2758\">#2758</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dc3d78dc228709c0968554694a884f9fe17a36bc\"><code>dc3d78d</code></a>\nfeat: [GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3469af7c272222e2ac9addd31d8c6e457c8ebb0c\"><code>3469af7</code></a>\nchore: internal testing</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/affa48ce7fac6a4d3495fa3fd83d4ee1b5c99752\"><code>affa48c</code></a>\nchore: internal change</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49059181ea0452e160ec61135c29f9c177f19160\"><code>4905918</code></a>\nfix: add deprecation warnings to Imagen generate_images, edit_images,\ngenerat...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/097a99e6c79f752af1ad055b6daffa384f6d6bc3\"><code>097a99e</code></a>\ndocs: Regenerate docs for 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/293238d4e516878b91d86bcddd9ee67f39d77b2d\"><code>293238d</code></a>\nchore: Internal change</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a381b8d60c9f737022106b98265f4995e41358d5\"><code>a381b8d</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.13.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2737\">#2737</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/87f1650e169a35cae45e415ad9b9c48e3e53f143\"><code>87f1650</code></a>\nfeat(interaction-api): add queued status to interaction proto</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7270e6d5c2854731e953fce04488fcf46bbb4c60\"><code>7270e6d</code></a>\nfeat: Support mTLS in custom client using google auth\nmtls.get_default_ssl_co...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.1...v2.14.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `openai` from 2.46.0 to 2.48.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/releases\">openai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.48.0</h2>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.47.0</h2>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and\nprivate-production-repo support in workflow templates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4303e974f08394789c6075b6745357b2f1c36e21\">4303e97</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\">d4dceb2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">openai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and\nprivate-production-repo support in workflow templates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4303e974f08394789c6075b6745357b2f1c36e21\">4303e97</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\">d4dceb2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/8a6adcb3b88d89462a0fc5a81f50d9775c9ca138\"><code>8a6adcb</code></a>\nrelease: 2.48.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/cbd2fba7c48b6376e80775cb191e2eda1d476c61\"><code>cbd2fba</code></a>\nfeat(api): add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin apis</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/00709f2ae951ce79705467e92d71a926a46b82f6\"><code>00709f2</code></a>\nfeat(api): accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/e67afa88433dad9f97e733ae8f2ee6e9c240bc51\"><code>e67afa8</code></a>\nrelease: 2.47.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/e1925e9804aa1bbd33359d91ed3fee105cac103f\"><code>e1925e9</code></a>\nfeat(client): Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2 clients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7f4edb662abdeb8178c9df48023975684aea4349\"><code>7f4edb6</code></a>\nfeat(stlc): configurable CI runner and private-production-repo support\nin wor...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\"><code>d4dceb2</code></a>\nfix(deps): require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/b140f45c2c1850306a91113245639a0a41f19f28\"><code>b140f45</code></a>\nci: Set up CodeQL scanning (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3514\">#3514</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.48.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cachetools` from 7.1.4 to 7.1.6\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">cachetools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v7.1.6 (2026-07-24)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor style improvements to keep <code>ruff</code> happy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v7.1.5 (2026-07-23)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix <code>TLRUCache</code> silently keeping stale values on expired\noverwrites.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Reject negative cache item <code>getsizeof</code> values.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Update build environment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/13bb86a55e36e501cf0b3e4c35db516ed9409fd7\"><code>13bb86a</code></a>\nMinor style improvements to keep ruff happy.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e2250be46b9d8ed76b82c1c18a4465c0b1167b8a\"><code>e2250be</code></a>\nFix RTD version handling.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/0d2a6ea17b3627bcf334c7360a8abe5889dd6235\"><code>0d2a6ea</code></a>\nRelease v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d64cf805de3c35feac4d2acc0d9d092bd9afd77e\"><code>d64cf80</code></a>\nPrepare v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/fcbb0de97fc09de646d2e210def765d07dee66e8\"><code>fcbb0de</code></a>\nFix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/406\">#406</a>:\nMerge branch 'gaoflow-fix-tlru-overwrite-expired-stale-value' into\n...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/c0fdf6abab38040947d6fe2e38c507401d5e2350\"><code>c0fdf6a</code></a>\nFix TLRUCache silently keeping stale value on expired overwrite</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/978d34d40cdbf3b4cbfce104f3166032cc4ea028\"><code>978d34d</code></a>\nBump actions/setup-python from 6.2.0 to 6.3.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d5c7eea7e52d18fed0ec1b575db1956b1d035782\"><code>d5c7eea</code></a>\nReject negative cache item sizes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/578e97648dd312880f8aea172437c6dd424d0028\"><code>578e976</code></a>\nUpdate build environment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e164b7020e4211b57d20fe2b252d931af6244ad4\"><code>e164b70</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/compare/v7.1.4...v7.1.6\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.15.22 to 0.16.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration guide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for more details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a full listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and <code>gitlab</code>\noutputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n<p>See the CLI help or <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#output-format\">documentation</a>\nfor the full list of supported formats.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <code>filename</code>, <code>location</code>,\n<code>end_location</code>, <code>fix.edits[].location</code>, and\n<code>fix.edits[].end_location</code> fields in the JSON output format\nmay now be <code>null</code> rather than defaulting to the empty string\nand row 1, column 1, respectively.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">ruff's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration\nguide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for\nmore details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a\nfull listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the\n<a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and\n<code>gitlab</code> outputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a2635fd8f39e1d34ce8074cb486809426148f3e9\"><code>a2635fd</code></a>\nBump 0.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27136\">#27136</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/34334491652f8ceca5246d15c5c5afe0d6bc77ae\"><code>3433449</code></a>\n[ty] Reuse full call diagnostics for implicit setter calls (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27115\">#27115</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/22400709220931375e072ad5d7460b9fc781af78\"><code>2240070</code></a>\nReflect <code>ruff: ignore</code> and <code>--add-ignore</code>\nstabilization in documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27\">#27</a>...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/17ef71142c52230b923dad46ee5554140fc3fd2e\"><code>17ef711</code></a>\nStabilize <code>--add-ignore</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27125\">#27125</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/ef912bbbe466856aa4aac10ad2a8856eb3d5aef3\"><code>ef912bb</code></a>\nAdd newly stabilized rules to defaults (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27055\">#27055</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/b30f04023281b46f12011f13ce6b45c247e0d2e3\"><code>b30f040</code></a>\nStabilize new default rules (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27035\">#27035</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/bcd70c5f10ea97ed52a785d70e7f33b83b7c697a\"><code>bcd70c5</code></a>\nExclude Markdown files from <code>format-dev</code> runs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27052\">#27052</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/87e51e2cbbaed376fc13dead40fd772361fa07c0\"><code>87e51e2</code></a>\nFix <code>format --check</code> spans for syntax errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27045\">#27045</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/afe2723a348364ac7f4b9abd76fc67779490c05e\"><code>afe2723</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-gettext</code>] Stabilize qualified-name and built-in\nbinding resolution (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a9702d8928344f77a41dbe535f655a69fb04e2df\"><code>a9702d8</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-bandit</code>] Stabilize string literal binding resolution\n(<code>S310</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26944\">#26944</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.15.22...0.16.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.139.2 to 0.140.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.140.0</h2>\n<h3>Refactors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16049\">#16049</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix links in docs. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15967\">#15967</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add Library Skills documentation. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16041\">#16041</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Update docs to use uv projects by default. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16032\">#16032</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Restructure FastAPI People and related pages. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16015\">#16015</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>👷 Add CI memory benchmark. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16046\">#16046</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👥 Update FastAPI People - Sponsors. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16027\">#16027</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔥 Remove now-obsolete scripts to generate data for FastAPI People.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16016\">#16016</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/255b912928904e3ba5980425a54d6837c8bd1a1c\"><code>255b912</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16050\">#16050</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/892eacd27dcdcfe6c5ea114543ff473cbbfd7c6f\"><code>892eacd</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/027082950068d6e3897b5422ab6cde3168f7d8b0\"><code>0270829</code></a>\n⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16049\">#16049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/ae031be7b5a2df589f63f4d25389cf07b7b8fc86\"><code>ae031be</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f3644b33cdaf1b14868d77f1c309e0a455c6bac8\"><code>f3644b3</code></a>\n📝 Fix links in docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15967\">#15967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1e24ca0e12e9a66cecb1e42780b9116374e2618d\"><code>1e24ca0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/513c396322664bcb3bdcb3946c440a8ed8ef080b\"><code>513c396</code></a>\n👷 Add CI memory benchmark (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16046\">#16046</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/a64dfbbd21a445288ff583d58e1f646fe6baf3af\"><code>a64dfbb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/4f155486f0c1465c5e1f8701544acc10cb8a78bb\"><code>4f15548</code></a>\n📝 Add Library Skills documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16041\">#16041</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/704fbe1439341994100622853f515a8af7ccc2eb\"><code>704fbe1</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.139.2...0.140.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cachetools` from 7.1.4 to 7.1.6\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">cachetools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v7.1.6 (2026-07-24)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor style improvements to keep <code>ruff</code> happy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v7.1.5 (2026-07-23)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix <code>TLRUCache</code> silently keeping stale values on expired\noverwrites.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Reject negative cache item <code>getsizeof</code> values.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Update build environment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/13bb86a55e36e501cf0b3e4c35db516ed9409fd7\"><code>13bb86a</code></a>\nMinor style improvements to keep ruff happy.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e2250be46b9d8ed76b82c1c18a4465c0b1167b8a\"><code>e2250be</code></a>\nFix RTD version handling.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/0d2a6ea17b3627bcf334c7360a8abe5889dd6235\"><code>0d2a6ea</code></a>\nRelease v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d64cf805de3c35feac4d2acc0d9d092bd9afd77e\"><code>d64cf80</code></a>\nPrepare v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/fcbb0de97fc09de646d2e210def765d07dee66e8\"><code>fcbb0de</code></a>\nFix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/406\">#406</a>:\nMerge branch 'gaoflow-fix-tlru-overwrite-expired-stale-value' into\n...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/c0fdf6abab38040947d6fe2e38c507401d5e2350\"><code>c0fdf6a</code></a>\nFix TLRUCache silently keeping stale value on expired overwrite</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/978d34d40cdbf3b4cbfce104f3166032cc4ea028\"><code>978d34d</code></a>\nBump actions/setup-python from 6.2.0 to 6.3.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d5c7eea7e52d18fed0ec1b575db1956b1d035782\"><code>d5c7eea</code></a>\nReject negative cache item sizes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/578e97648dd312880f8aea172437c6dd424d0028\"><code>578e976</code></a>\nUpdate build environment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e164b7020e4211b57d20fe2b252d931af6244ad4\"><code>e164b70</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/compare/v7.1.4...v7.1.6\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.15.22 to 0.16.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration guide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for more details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a full listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and <code>gitlab</code>\noutputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n<p>See the CLI help or <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#output-format\">documentation</a>\nfor the full list of supported formats.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <code>filename</code>, <code>location</code>,\n<code>end_location</code>, <code>fix.edits[].location</code>, and\n<code>fix.edits[].end_location</code> fields in the JSON output format\nmay now be <code>null</code> rather than defaulting to the empty string\nand row 1, column 1, respectively.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">ruff's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration\nguide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for\nmore details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a\nfull listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the\n<a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and\n<code>gitlab</code> outputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a2635fd8f39e1d34ce8074cb486809426148f3e9\"><code>a2635fd</code></a>\nBump 0.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27136\">#27136</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/34334491652f8ceca5246d15c5c5afe0d6bc77ae\"><code>3433449</code></a>\n[ty] Reuse full call diagnostics for implicit setter calls (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27115\">#27115</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/22400709220931375e072ad5d7460b9fc781af78\"><code>2240070</code></a>\nReflect <code>ruff: ignore</code> and <code>--add-ignore</code>\nstabilization in documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27\">#27</a>...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/17ef71142c52230b923dad46ee5554140fc3fd2e\"><code>17ef711</code></a>\nStabilize <code>--add-ignore</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27125\">#27125</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/ef912bbbe466856aa4aac10ad2a8856eb3d5aef3\"><code>ef912bb</code></a>\nAdd newly stabilized rules to defaults (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27055\">#27055</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/b30f04023281b46f12011f13ce6b45c247e0d2e3\"><code>b30f040</code></a>\nStabilize new default rules (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27035\">#27035</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/bcd70c5f10ea97ed52a785d70e7f33b83b7c697a\"><code>bcd70c5</code></a>\nExclude Markdown files from <code>format-dev</code> runs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27052\">#27052</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/87e51e2cbbaed376fc13dead40fd772361fa07c0\"><code>87e51e2</code></a>\nFix <code>format --check</code> spans for syntax errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27045\">#27045</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/afe2723a348364ac7f4b9abd76fc67779490c05e\"><code>afe2723</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-gettext</code>] Stabilize qualified-name and built-in\nbinding resolution (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a9702d8928344f77a41dbe535f655a69fb04e2df\"><code>a9702d8</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-bandit</code>] Stabilize string literal binding resolution\n(<code>S310</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26944\">#26944</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.15.22...0.16.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.139.2 to 0.140.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.140.0</h2>\n<h3>Refactors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16049\">#16049</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix links in docs. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15967\">#15967</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add Library Skills documentation. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16041\">#16041</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Update docs to use uv projects by default. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16032\">#16032</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Restructure FastAPI People and related pages. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16015\">#16015</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>👷 Add CI memory benchmark. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16046\">#16046</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👥 Update FastAPI People - Sponsors. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16027\">#16027</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔥 Remove now-obsolete scripts to generate data for FastAPI People.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16016\">#16016</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/255b912928904e3ba5980425a54d6837c8bd1a1c\"><code>255b912</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16050\">#16050</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/892eacd27dcdcfe6c5ea114543ff473cbbfd7c6f\"><code>892eacd</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/027082950068d6e3897b5422ab6cde3168f7d8b0\"><code>0270829</code></a>\n⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16049\">#16049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/ae031be7b5a2df589f63f4d25389cf07b7b8fc86\"><code>ae031be</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f3644b33cdaf1b14868d77f1c309e0a455c6bac8\"><code>f3644b3</code></a>\n📝 Fix links in docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15967\">#15967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1e24ca0e12e9a66cecb1e42780b9116374e2618d\"><code>1e24ca0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/513c396322664bcb3bdcb3946c440a8ed8ef080b\"><code>513c396</code></a>\n👷 Add CI memory benchmark (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16046\">#16046</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/a64dfbbd21a445288ff583d58e1f646fe6baf3af\"><code>a64dfbb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/4f155486f0c1465c5e1f8701544acc10cb8a78bb\"><code>4f15548</code></a>\n📝 Add Library Skills documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16041\">#16041</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/704fbe1439341994100622853f515a8af7ccc2eb\"><code>704fbe1</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.139.2...0.140.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `greenlet` from 3.5.3 to 3.5.4\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/blob/master/CHANGES.rst\">greenlet's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>3.5.4 (2026-07-22)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a crash (segfault) on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14 and\nlater when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet that was\nstarted from a non-empty C-stack-reference state is active.\nSee <code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a potential use-after-free on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14\nand later when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet is\nsuspended holding a <code>_PyCStackRef</code> (for example, mid\nattribute\nresolution). See\n<code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a deadlock on free-threaded builds when a greenlet switch\nhappened\nwhile a <code>PyCriticalSection</code> was held -- for example inside\nasyncio's\n<code>Task.__step</code>, which holds one on the running task for the\nduration of\nthe step. See <code>PR 519\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/pull/519/&gt;</code>.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. note::\nBinary 3.15 wheels are now built with Python 3.15b4. These may not\nbe compatible with earlier or later versions of 3.15. Binary\n3.15 wheels of greenlet from previous releases (e.g., 3.5.3)\nmay not be compatible with Python 3.15b4.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/384be8821a934fbb835e369dda2b9b72107e80be\"><code>384be88</code></a>\nPreparing release 3.5.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/bbdf57b8cccc572639103005bc7dee41d1c309a2\"><code>bbdf57b</code></a>\nAdd note to CHANGES about versions of 3.15 binary wheels may/not be\ncompatibl...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/759902381a85e2ebca2102fab50ffb99b2227a2b\"><code>7599023</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/517\">#517</a>\nfrom ddorian/issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/73a0a1aadf8d45db71754954d588d433fa826a2a\"><code>73a0a1a</code></a>\nFix the suspended C-stack-ref GC test to catch its regression</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/1ff35f431f768e854db323ae14274044a06d9d12\"><code>1ff35f4</code></a>\nMerge branch 'master' into issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/847fb824f6c0590d87963c38c4b2f452a0980b37\"><code>847fb82</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/520\">#520</a>\nfrom dynapx/fix-test-extension-npd</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/0b471ba66bed12fcf7bef969f26705a30a29a5b4\"><code>0b471ba</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/519\">#519</a>\nfrom ddorian/freethread-switch-critical-section</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/d55914df27b30af452e63eb2be41fc9b3ec2c982\"><code>d55914d</code></a>\nSimplify the CHANGES.rst entry</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/78932dc67b6571a920751339cfd88056144e8116\"><code>78932dc</code></a>\nChange notes are for end users, they don't need to go into technical\ndetail</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/39bf70c2cb8c8996ce26bc20e4161fd94c05d380\"><code>39bf70c</code></a>\nHold the C-stack ref snapshot in a std::vector&lt;OwnedObject&gt;</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/compare/3.5.3...3.5.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `openai` from 2.46.0 to 2.48.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/releases\">openai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.48.0</h2>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.47.0</h2>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and\nprivate-production-repo support in workflow templates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4303e974f08394789c6075b6745357b2f1c36e21\">4303e97</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\">d4dceb2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">openai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\n…","tree":{"sha":"4fd9ea6f8695d8c0dab14deaffda46f78002186e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/4fd9ea6f8695d8c0dab14deaffda46f78002186e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZyzgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO2kQAJg/iW6X4HqzDyyekHChKvGt\n3WKarVLefeHoSm/kinighIXNd5YeXeCWl9/9q+cPFdkBAru7l3z+oDd6h0nxQZNS\nLih2sZ5NF+uq7fsvDs1jjjIs0DlcKVYrqwdc7k13yO3fFl05rV6fuursnfD9hHif\nTE/PDbW9yenVOlTfwcYCFJBdw3F/ch0igMLMSoapHqc2Yq8DfSyg5yxWyOQItWVj\ntAKi7j3PVJs5Vs0MVKPvZ1/nOhFV33fvzMC0pwRuX8KzjKoyy0Ox9N0AM0885Fc2\n73M6cmdra4nzzs+N0DIEsDhke+gxQh0qtsBZZtFLPq1d2/ML3b/hbcXfbyR0GGC2\nbI8SUobshKdxgqnJCumf5MJuLrAyajvyO8cCOdIstcCoYv1QDuzZjYcI1/xdXnGJ\nA/+rIpm+69ywIe2bQ2z/iwd/aoB5KGHduRRWKJOwaTo+D+Jp1csjroQvdRDiCSf0\nRJwdNqsJdX6rXF5yWTPY4SBo/CFCUyl0JnaGdDqo15jxU7+tjh4ChnrQ7LOgB/7T\ng92KypjpR0bJ6Tk6nRIOhxUvqFpH0hLEV4ATjOAyoEwCVY0bJ9mwpT7LG3TBiXNW\n5fcg0nWajgXFiTHYq1/Q+wXht2q51RB09ubLiv3DMRNv5KAG50xur4xhAy5yqbNE\nF37/SgbXyHF1Y4enSVqe\n=2J/1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4fd9ea6f8695d8c0dab14deaffda46f78002186e\nparent 49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785146592 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785146592 +0300\n\ndeps: bump the uv-minor-patch group across 4 directories with 8 updates (#649)\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 7 updates in the /core-api\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.139.2` | `0.140.0`\n|\n| [greenlet](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet) | `3.5.3` |\n`3.5.4` |\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.161.0` | `1.162.0` |\n| [google-genai](https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai) | `2.12.1`\n| `2.14.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.46.0` |\n`2.48.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.4` | `7.1.6` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.15.22` | `0.16.0` |\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 3 updates in the /core-operations\ndirectory: [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi),\n[cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) and\n[ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 4 updates in the /core-storage-api\ndirectory: [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi),\n[greenlet](https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet),\n[openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) and\n[ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 6 updates in the /core-worker\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.139.2` | `0.140.0`\n|\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.161.0` | `1.162.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.46.0` |\n`2.48.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.4` | `7.1.6` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.15.22` | `0.16.0` |\n|\n[sentence-transformers](https://github.com/huggingface/sentence-transformers)\n| `5.6.0` | `5.6.1` |\n\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.139.2 to 0.140.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.140.0</h2>\n<h3>Refactors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16049\">#16049</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix links in docs. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15967\">#15967</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add Library Skills documentation. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16041\">#16041</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Update docs to use uv projects by default. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16032\">#16032</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Restructure FastAPI People and related pages. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16015\">#16015</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>👷 Add CI memory benchmark. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16046\">#16046</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👥 Update FastAPI People - Sponsors. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16027\">#16027</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔥 Remove now-obsolete scripts to generate data for FastAPI People.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16016\">#16016</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/255b912928904e3ba5980425a54d6837c8bd1a1c\"><code>255b912</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16050\">#16050</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/892eacd27dcdcfe6c5ea114543ff473cbbfd7c6f\"><code>892eacd</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/027082950068d6e3897b5422ab6cde3168f7d8b0\"><code>0270829</code></a>\n⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16049\">#16049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/ae031be7b5a2df589f63f4d25389cf07b7b8fc86\"><code>ae031be</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f3644b33cdaf1b14868d77f1c309e0a455c6bac8\"><code>f3644b3</code></a>\n📝 Fix links in docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15967\">#15967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1e24ca0e12e9a66cecb1e42780b9116374e2618d\"><code>1e24ca0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/513c396322664bcb3bdcb3946c440a8ed8ef080b\"><code>513c396</code></a>\n👷 Add CI memory benchmark (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16046\">#16046</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/a64dfbbd21a445288ff583d58e1f646fe6baf3af\"><code>a64dfbb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/4f155486f0c1465c5e1f8701544acc10cb8a78bb\"><code>4f15548</code></a>\n📝 Add Library Skills documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16041\">#16041</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/704fbe1439341994100622853f515a8af7ccc2eb\"><code>704fbe1</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.139.2...0.140.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `greenlet` from 3.5.3 to 3.5.4\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/blob/master/CHANGES.rst\">greenlet's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>3.5.4 (2026-07-22)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a crash (segfault) on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14 and\nlater when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet that was\nstarted from a non-empty C-stack-reference state is active.\nSee <code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a potential use-after-free on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14\nand later when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet is\nsuspended holding a <code>_PyCStackRef</code> (for example, mid\nattribute\nresolution). See\n<code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a deadlock on free-threaded builds when a greenlet switch\nhappened\nwhile a <code>PyCriticalSection</code> was held -- for example inside\nasyncio's\n<code>Task.__step</code>, which holds one on the running task for the\nduration of\nthe step. See <code>PR 519\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/pull/519/&gt;</code>.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. note::\nBinary 3.15 wheels are now built with Python 3.15b4. These may not\nbe compatible with earlier or later versions of 3.15. Binary\n3.15 wheels of greenlet from previous releases (e.g., 3.5.3)\nmay not be compatible with Python 3.15b4.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/384be8821a934fbb835e369dda2b9b72107e80be\"><code>384be88</code></a>\nPreparing release 3.5.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/bbdf57b8cccc572639103005bc7dee41d1c309a2\"><code>bbdf57b</code></a>\nAdd note to CHANGES about versions of 3.15 binary wheels may/not be\ncompatibl...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/759902381a85e2ebca2102fab50ffb99b2227a2b\"><code>7599023</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/517\">#517</a>\nfrom ddorian/issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/73a0a1aadf8d45db71754954d588d433fa826a2a\"><code>73a0a1a</code></a>\nFix the suspended C-stack-ref GC test to catch its regression</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/1ff35f431f768e854db323ae14274044a06d9d12\"><code>1ff35f4</code></a>\nMerge branch 'master' into issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/847fb824f6c0590d87963c38c4b2f452a0980b37\"><code>847fb82</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/520\">#520</a>\nfrom dynapx/fix-test-extension-npd</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/0b471ba66bed12fcf7bef969f26705a30a29a5b4\"><code>0b471ba</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/519\">#519</a>\nfrom ddorian/freethread-switch-critical-section</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/d55914df27b30af452e63eb2be41fc9b3ec2c982\"><code>d55914d</code></a>\nSimplify the CHANGES.rst entry</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/78932dc67b6571a920751339cfd88056144e8116\"><code>78932dc</code></a>\nChange notes are for end users, they don't need to go into technical\ndetail</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/39bf70c2cb8c8996ce26bc20e4161fd94c05d380\"><code>39bf70c</code></a>\nHold the C-stack ref snapshot in a std::vector&lt;OwnedObject&gt;</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/compare/3.5.3...3.5.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-cloud-aiplatform` from 1.161.0 to 1.162.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/releases\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.162.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.161.0...v1.162.0\">1.162.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add detailed agent tool definitions for display (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/762079f098e21fff5f914b760671ff2cc1647567\">762079f</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1beta1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Delegate agent resolution to server via geminiAgentConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ab757c7d86f10d38438f9dda50daaa3521b46b29\">ab757c7</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add warning on vertexai.Client instantiation and\nrecommend agentplatform.Client (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f141415043dc9c3d3cdb5850263869b1d6974f3f\">f141415</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - multi-turn user simulation for Gemini Agents\nAPI run_inference (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c74e996d09e7633e7bd66a06df24ecff9224846b\">c74e996</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the correct enum for RagFile.file_status (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/23145f30843febc29cc607930df02b1e083ce39a\">23145f3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add example usage to RAG docstrings (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df3dcd976330f0de50537569d76d9aef1337ed74\">df3dcd9</a>)</li>\n<li>Update product name from &quot;Vertex AI&quot; to &quot;Gemini\nEnterprise Agent Platform&quot; in README, and add a note to rename\nAgent Engine to Agent Runtime in upcoming major release (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a3179c2c7f0480b0d9abe3e205edd7e402ad5f2b\">a3179c2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.161.0...v1.162.0\">1.162.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add detailed agent tool definitions for display (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/762079f098e21fff5f914b760671ff2cc1647567\">762079f</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Add Route to GroundingChunk.Maps in Vertex AI v1beta1 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Delegate agent resolution to server via geminiAgentConfig (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ab757c7d86f10d38438f9dda50daaa3521b46b29\">ab757c7</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add warning on vertexai.Client instantiation and\nrecommend agentplatform.Client (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f141415043dc9c3d3cdb5850263869b1d6974f3f\">f141415</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - multi-turn user simulation for Gemini Agents\nAPI run_inference (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c74e996d09e7633e7bd66a06df24ecff9224846b\">c74e996</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the correct enum for RagFile.file_status (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/23145f30843febc29cc607930df02b1e083ce39a\">23145f3</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>Expand GroundingChunk.Maps documentation to describe route support\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\">4331d55</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Add example usage to RAG docstrings (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df3dcd976330f0de50537569d76d9aef1337ed74\">df3dcd9</a>)</li>\n<li>Update product name from &quot;Vertex AI&quot; to &quot;Gemini\nEnterprise Agent Platform&quot; in README, and add a note to rename\nAgent Engine to Agent Runtime in upcoming major release (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a3179c2c7f0480b0d9abe3e205edd7e402ad5f2b\">a3179c2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/922fa6ae798d3d753426ef2572aaf3574c0a4066\"><code>922fa6a</code></a>\nchore(main): release 1.162.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/issues/7003\">#7003</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/4331d55ea3e388a8bb0d548015b5d819ce65394a\"><code>4331d55</code></a>\nCopybara import of the project:</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/06a9089fc5ca2c53656bd05028814f5c4e06b11c\"><code>06a9089</code></a>\nchore: Handle interactions_data_source as a valid data source</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/ab757c7d86f10d38438f9dda50daaa3521b46b29\"><code>ab757c7</code></a>\nfeat: Delegate agent resolution to server via geminiAgentConfig</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/762079f098e21fff5f914b760671ff2cc1647567\"><code>762079f</code></a>\nfeat: Add detailed agent tool definitions for display</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f141415043dc9c3d3cdb5850263869b1d6974f3f\"><code>f141415</code></a>\nfeat: GenAI client - Add warning on vertexai.Client instantiation and\nrecomme...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/23145f30843febc29cc607930df02b1e083ce39a\"><code>23145f3</code></a>\nfix: Use the correct enum for RagFile.file_status</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/df3dcd976330f0de50537569d76d9aef1337ed74\"><code>df3dcd9</code></a>\ndocs: GenAI client - Add example usage to RAG docstrings</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/62bc783b94763bb1e49c0f33b5b9ebcee1d3aa55\"><code>62bc783</code></a>\nchore: Add a2a framework test to agentplatform.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a3179c2c7f0480b0d9abe3e205edd7e402ad5f2b\"><code>a3179c2</code></a>\ndocs: Update product name from &quot;Vertex AI&quot; to &quot;Gemini\nEnterprise Agent Platfo...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.161.0...v1.162.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-genai` from 2.12.1 to 2.14.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/releases\">google-genai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.14.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.13.0...v2.14.0\">2.14.0</a>\n(2026-07-22)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config and\nPart.audio_transcription. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dc3d78dc228709c0968554694a884f9fe17a36bc\">dc3d78d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add deprecation warnings to Imagen generate_images, edit_images,\ngenerate_videos (if using prompt/text/image args),\nLiveConnectConfig.GenerationConfig which will be removed in the next\nmajor version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49059181ea0452e160ec61135c29f9c177f19160\">4905918</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.13.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/097a99e6c79f752af1ad055b6daffa384f6d6bc3\">097a99e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.13.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.1...v2.13.0\">2.13.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A new field <code>custom_vocabulary</code> is added to to Live API\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/4eeb1ade8dedb9ccdabe00892d4ff2119b54a444\">4eeb1ad</a>)</li>\n<li>Add model selector (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/bf3dba460092d2f3af7a2b29abe2f0778ff8334d\">bf3dba4</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interaction-api:</strong> Add queued status to interaction\nproto (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/87f1650e169a35cae45e415ad9b9c48e3e53f143\">87f1650</a>)</li>\n<li>Make ASR fields public in v1main and Interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/5b52faaca37744c6a79b2bb37b3204229c445121\">5b52faa</a>)</li>\n<li>Support mTLS in custom client using google auth\nmtls.get_default_ssl_context (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7270e6d5c2854731e953fce04488fcf46bbb4c60\">7270e6d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.11.0 and 2.12.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dddd7c6a2e7b3f3eabcda4417ebb5fa1a0207526\">dddd7c6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-genai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.13.0...v2.14.0\">2.14.0</a>\n(2026-07-22)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config and\nPart.audio_transcription. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dc3d78dc228709c0968554694a884f9fe17a36bc\">dc3d78d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add deprecation warnings to Imagen generate_images, edit_images,\ngenerate_videos (if using prompt/text/image args),\nLiveConnectConfig.GenerationConfig which will be removed in the next\nmajor version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49059181ea0452e160ec61135c29f9c177f19160\">4905918</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.13.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/097a99e6c79f752af1ad055b6daffa384f6d6bc3\">097a99e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.1...v2.13.0\">2.13.0</a>\n(2026-07-21)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A new field <code>custom_vocabulary</code> is added to message\n<code>.google.cloud.aiplatform.v1beta1.BidiGenerateContentSetup</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/4eeb1ade8dedb9ccdabe00892d4ff2119b54a444\">4eeb1ad</a>)</li>\n<li>Add model selector (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/bf3dba460092d2f3af7a2b29abe2f0778ff8334d\">bf3dba4</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>interaction-api:</strong> Add queued status to interaction\nproto (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/87f1650e169a35cae45e415ad9b9c48e3e53f143\">87f1650</a>)</li>\n<li>Make ASR fields public in v1main and Interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/5b52faaca37744c6a79b2bb37b3204229c445121\">5b52faa</a>)</li>\n<li>Support mTLS in custom client using google auth\nmtls.get_default_ssl_context (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7270e6d5c2854731e953fce04488fcf46bbb4c60\">7270e6d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.11.0 and 2.12.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dddd7c6a2e7b3f3eabcda4417ebb5fa1a0207526\">dddd7c6</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7c1f70d4103deed1b210a2c3cfe3b155defd672e\"><code>7c1f70d</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.14.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2758\">#2758</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/dc3d78dc228709c0968554694a884f9fe17a36bc\"><code>dc3d78d</code></a>\nfeat: [GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3469af7c272222e2ac9addd31d8c6e457c8ebb0c\"><code>3469af7</code></a>\nchore: internal testing</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/affa48ce7fac6a4d3495fa3fd83d4ee1b5c99752\"><code>affa48c</code></a>\nchore: internal change</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49059181ea0452e160ec61135c29f9c177f19160\"><code>4905918</code></a>\nfix: add deprecation warnings to Imagen generate_images, edit_images,\ngenerat...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/097a99e6c79f752af1ad055b6daffa384f6d6bc3\"><code>097a99e</code></a>\ndocs: Regenerate docs for 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/293238d4e516878b91d86bcddd9ee67f39d77b2d\"><code>293238d</code></a>\nchore: Internal change</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a381b8d60c9f737022106b98265f4995e41358d5\"><code>a381b8d</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.13.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2737\">#2737</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/87f1650e169a35cae45e415ad9b9c48e3e53f143\"><code>87f1650</code></a>\nfeat(interaction-api): add queued status to interaction proto</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7270e6d5c2854731e953fce04488fcf46bbb4c60\"><code>7270e6d</code></a>\nfeat: Support mTLS in custom client using google auth\nmtls.get_default_ssl_co...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.12.1...v2.14.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `openai` from 2.46.0 to 2.48.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/releases\">openai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.48.0</h2>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.47.0</h2>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and\nprivate-production-repo support in workflow templates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4303e974f08394789c6075b6745357b2f1c36e21\">4303e97</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\">d4dceb2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">openai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and\nprivate-production-repo support in workflow templates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4303e974f08394789c6075b6745357b2f1c36e21\">4303e97</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\">d4dceb2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/8a6adcb3b88d89462a0fc5a81f50d9775c9ca138\"><code>8a6adcb</code></a>\nrelease: 2.48.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/cbd2fba7c48b6376e80775cb191e2eda1d476c61\"><code>cbd2fba</code></a>\nfeat(api): add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin apis</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/00709f2ae951ce79705467e92d71a926a46b82f6\"><code>00709f2</code></a>\nfeat(api): accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/e67afa88433dad9f97e733ae8f2ee6e9c240bc51\"><code>e67afa8</code></a>\nrelease: 2.47.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/e1925e9804aa1bbd33359d91ed3fee105cac103f\"><code>e1925e9</code></a>\nfeat(client): Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2 clients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7f4edb662abdeb8178c9df48023975684aea4349\"><code>7f4edb6</code></a>\nfeat(stlc): configurable CI runner and private-production-repo support\nin wor...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\"><code>d4dceb2</code></a>\nfix(deps): require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/b140f45c2c1850306a91113245639a0a41f19f28\"><code>b140f45</code></a>\nci: Set up CodeQL scanning (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3514\">#3514</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.48.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cachetools` from 7.1.4 to 7.1.6\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">cachetools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v7.1.6 (2026-07-24)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor style improvements to keep <code>ruff</code> happy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v7.1.5 (2026-07-23)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix <code>TLRUCache</code> silently keeping stale values on expired\noverwrites.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Reject negative cache item <code>getsizeof</code> values.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Update build environment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/13bb86a55e36e501cf0b3e4c35db516ed9409fd7\"><code>13bb86a</code></a>\nMinor style improvements to keep ruff happy.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e2250be46b9d8ed76b82c1c18a4465c0b1167b8a\"><code>e2250be</code></a>\nFix RTD version handling.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/0d2a6ea17b3627bcf334c7360a8abe5889dd6235\"><code>0d2a6ea</code></a>\nRelease v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d64cf805de3c35feac4d2acc0d9d092bd9afd77e\"><code>d64cf80</code></a>\nPrepare v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/fcbb0de97fc09de646d2e210def765d07dee66e8\"><code>fcbb0de</code></a>\nFix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/406\">#406</a>:\nMerge branch 'gaoflow-fix-tlru-overwrite-expired-stale-value' into\n...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/c0fdf6abab38040947d6fe2e38c507401d5e2350\"><code>c0fdf6a</code></a>\nFix TLRUCache silently keeping stale value on expired overwrite</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/978d34d40cdbf3b4cbfce104f3166032cc4ea028\"><code>978d34d</code></a>\nBump actions/setup-python from 6.2.0 to 6.3.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d5c7eea7e52d18fed0ec1b575db1956b1d035782\"><code>d5c7eea</code></a>\nReject negative cache item sizes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/578e97648dd312880f8aea172437c6dd424d0028\"><code>578e976</code></a>\nUpdate build environment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e164b7020e4211b57d20fe2b252d931af6244ad4\"><code>e164b70</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/compare/v7.1.4...v7.1.6\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.15.22 to 0.16.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration guide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for more details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a full listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and <code>gitlab</code>\noutputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n<p>See the CLI help or <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#output-format\">documentation</a>\nfor the full list of supported formats.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <code>filename</code>, <code>location</code>,\n<code>end_location</code>, <code>fix.edits[].location</code>, and\n<code>fix.edits[].end_location</code> fields in the JSON output format\nmay now be <code>null</code> rather than defaulting to the empty string\nand row 1, column 1, respectively.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">ruff's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration\nguide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for\nmore details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a\nfull listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the\n<a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and\n<code>gitlab</code> outputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a2635fd8f39e1d34ce8074cb486809426148f3e9\"><code>a2635fd</code></a>\nBump 0.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27136\">#27136</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/34334491652f8ceca5246d15c5c5afe0d6bc77ae\"><code>3433449</code></a>\n[ty] Reuse full call diagnostics for implicit setter calls (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27115\">#27115</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/22400709220931375e072ad5d7460b9fc781af78\"><code>2240070</code></a>\nReflect <code>ruff: ignore</code> and <code>--add-ignore</code>\nstabilization in documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27\">#27</a>...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/17ef71142c52230b923dad46ee5554140fc3fd2e\"><code>17ef711</code></a>\nStabilize <code>--add-ignore</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27125\">#27125</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/ef912bbbe466856aa4aac10ad2a8856eb3d5aef3\"><code>ef912bb</code></a>\nAdd newly stabilized rules to defaults (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27055\">#27055</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/b30f04023281b46f12011f13ce6b45c247e0d2e3\"><code>b30f040</code></a>\nStabilize new default rules (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27035\">#27035</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/bcd70c5f10ea97ed52a785d70e7f33b83b7c697a\"><code>bcd70c5</code></a>\nExclude Markdown files from <code>format-dev</code> runs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27052\">#27052</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/87e51e2cbbaed376fc13dead40fd772361fa07c0\"><code>87e51e2</code></a>\nFix <code>format --check</code> spans for syntax errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27045\">#27045</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/afe2723a348364ac7f4b9abd76fc67779490c05e\"><code>afe2723</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-gettext</code>] Stabilize qualified-name and built-in\nbinding resolution (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a9702d8928344f77a41dbe535f655a69fb04e2df\"><code>a9702d8</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-bandit</code>] Stabilize string literal binding resolution\n(<code>S310</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26944\">#26944</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.15.22...0.16.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.139.2 to 0.140.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.140.0</h2>\n<h3>Refactors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16049\">#16049</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix links in docs. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15967\">#15967</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add Library Skills documentation. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16041\">#16041</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Update docs to use uv projects by default. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16032\">#16032</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Restructure FastAPI People and related pages. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16015\">#16015</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>👷 Add CI memory benchmark. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16046\">#16046</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👥 Update FastAPI People - Sponsors. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16027\">#16027</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔥 Remove now-obsolete scripts to generate data for FastAPI People.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16016\">#16016</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/255b912928904e3ba5980425a54d6837c8bd1a1c\"><code>255b912</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16050\">#16050</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/892eacd27dcdcfe6c5ea114543ff473cbbfd7c6f\"><code>892eacd</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/027082950068d6e3897b5422ab6cde3168f7d8b0\"><code>0270829</code></a>\n⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16049\">#16049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/ae031be7b5a2df589f63f4d25389cf07b7b8fc86\"><code>ae031be</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f3644b33cdaf1b14868d77f1c309e0a455c6bac8\"><code>f3644b3</code></a>\n📝 Fix links in docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15967\">#15967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1e24ca0e12e9a66cecb1e42780b9116374e2618d\"><code>1e24ca0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/513c396322664bcb3bdcb3946c440a8ed8ef080b\"><code>513c396</code></a>\n👷 Add CI memory benchmark (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16046\">#16046</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/a64dfbbd21a445288ff583d58e1f646fe6baf3af\"><code>a64dfbb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/4f155486f0c1465c5e1f8701544acc10cb8a78bb\"><code>4f15548</code></a>\n📝 Add Library Skills documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16041\">#16041</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/704fbe1439341994100622853f515a8af7ccc2eb\"><code>704fbe1</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.139.2...0.140.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cachetools` from 7.1.4 to 7.1.6\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">cachetools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v7.1.6 (2026-07-24)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor style improvements to keep <code>ruff</code> happy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>v7.1.5 (2026-07-23)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix <code>TLRUCache</code> silently keeping stale values on expired\noverwrites.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Reject negative cache item <code>getsizeof</code> values.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Update build environment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/13bb86a55e36e501cf0b3e4c35db516ed9409fd7\"><code>13bb86a</code></a>\nMinor style improvements to keep ruff happy.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e2250be46b9d8ed76b82c1c18a4465c0b1167b8a\"><code>e2250be</code></a>\nFix RTD version handling.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/0d2a6ea17b3627bcf334c7360a8abe5889dd6235\"><code>0d2a6ea</code></a>\nRelease v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d64cf805de3c35feac4d2acc0d9d092bd9afd77e\"><code>d64cf80</code></a>\nPrepare v7.1.5.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/fcbb0de97fc09de646d2e210def765d07dee66e8\"><code>fcbb0de</code></a>\nFix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/406\">#406</a>:\nMerge branch 'gaoflow-fix-tlru-overwrite-expired-stale-value' into\n...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/c0fdf6abab38040947d6fe2e38c507401d5e2350\"><code>c0fdf6a</code></a>\nFix TLRUCache silently keeping stale value on expired overwrite</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/978d34d40cdbf3b4cbfce104f3166032cc4ea028\"><code>978d34d</code></a>\nBump actions/setup-python from 6.2.0 to 6.3.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/d5c7eea7e52d18fed0ec1b575db1956b1d035782\"><code>d5c7eea</code></a>\nReject negative cache item sizes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/578e97648dd312880f8aea172437c6dd424d0028\"><code>578e976</code></a>\nUpdate build environment.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/e164b7020e4211b57d20fe2b252d931af6244ad4\"><code>e164b70</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/compare/v7.1.4...v7.1.6\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.15.22 to 0.16.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration guide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for more details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a full listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and <code>gitlab</code>\noutputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n<p>See the CLI help or <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#output-format\">documentation</a>\nfor the full list of supported formats.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <code>filename</code>, <code>location</code>,\n<code>end_location</code>, <code>fix.edits[].location</code>, and\n<code>fix.edits[].end_location</code> fields in the JSON output format\nmay now be <code>null</code> rather than defaulting to the empty string\nand row 1, column 1, respectively.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">ruff's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.0</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-07-23.</p>\n<p>Check out the <a href=\"https://astral.sh/blog/ruff-v0.16.0\">blog\npost</a> for a migration\nguide and overview of the changes!</p>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now enables a much larger set of rules by default (413, up from\n59). See the blog post for\nmore details and the new <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/default-rules/\">Default Rules</a> page\nfor a\nfull listing of the enabled rules.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff can now format Python code blocks in Markdown files and will do\nthis by default. See the\n<a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/#markdown-code-formatting\">documentation</a>\nfor more details.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ruff now supports <code>ruff: ignore</code> comments at the ends of\nlines, like <code>noqa</code> comments, or on the line preceding a\ndiagnostic. For example, these both suppress an <a\nhref=\"https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/\"><code>unused-import</code></a>\n(<code>F401</code>) diagnostic:</p>\n<pre lang=\"py\"><code>import math  # ruff: ignore[F401]\n<h1>ruff: ignore[F401]</h1>\n<p>import os\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fixes are now shown in <code>check</code> and <code>format\n--check</code> output:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check .\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n --&gt; try.md:1:1\n  |\n1 | ```python\n  - import   math\n2 + import math\n3 | ```\n  |\n<p>1 file would be reformatted\n</code></pre></p>\n<p>This example also shows off the Markdown formatting.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>format --check</code> now supports the same output formats as\nthe linter, including the <code>github</code> and\n<code>gitlab</code> outputs for rendering annotations in CI:</p>\n<pre lang=\"console\"><code>❯ ruff format --check --output-format github .\n::error title=ruff\n(unformatted),file=try.md,line=2,col=8,endLine=2,endColumn=10::try.md:2:8:\nunformatted: File would be reformatted\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a2635fd8f39e1d34ce8074cb486809426148f3e9\"><code>a2635fd</code></a>\nBump 0.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27136\">#27136</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/34334491652f8ceca5246d15c5c5afe0d6bc77ae\"><code>3433449</code></a>\n[ty] Reuse full call diagnostics for implicit setter calls (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27115\">#27115</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/22400709220931375e072ad5d7460b9fc781af78\"><code>2240070</code></a>\nReflect <code>ruff: ignore</code> and <code>--add-ignore</code>\nstabilization in documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27\">#27</a>...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/17ef71142c52230b923dad46ee5554140fc3fd2e\"><code>17ef711</code></a>\nStabilize <code>--add-ignore</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27125\">#27125</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/ef912bbbe466856aa4aac10ad2a8856eb3d5aef3\"><code>ef912bb</code></a>\nAdd newly stabilized rules to defaults (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27055\">#27055</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/b30f04023281b46f12011f13ce6b45c247e0d2e3\"><code>b30f040</code></a>\nStabilize new default rules (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27035\">#27035</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/bcd70c5f10ea97ed52a785d70e7f33b83b7c697a\"><code>bcd70c5</code></a>\nExclude Markdown files from <code>format-dev</code> runs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27052\">#27052</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/87e51e2cbbaed376fc13dead40fd772361fa07c0\"><code>87e51e2</code></a>\nFix <code>format --check</code> spans for syntax errors (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/27045\">#27045</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/afe2723a348364ac7f4b9abd76fc67779490c05e\"><code>afe2723</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-gettext</code>] Stabilize qualified-name and built-in\nbinding resolution (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/commit/a9702d8928344f77a41dbe535f655a69fb04e2df\"><code>a9702d8</code></a>\n[<code>flake8-bandit</code>] Stabilize string literal binding resolution\n(<code>S310</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/26944\">#26944</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.15.22...0.16.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.139.2 to 0.140.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.140.0</h2>\n<h3>Refactors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16049\">#16049</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix links in docs. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15967\">#15967</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add Library Skills documentation. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16041\">#16041</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Update docs to use uv projects by default. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16032\">#16032</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Restructure FastAPI People and related pages. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16015\">#16015</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>👷 Add CI memory benchmark. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16046\">#16046</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>👥 Update FastAPI People - Sponsors. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16027\">#16027</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🔥 Remove now-obsolete scripts to generate data for FastAPI People.\nPR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16016\">#16016</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/255b912928904e3ba5980425a54d6837c8bd1a1c\"><code>255b912</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16050\">#16050</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/892eacd27dcdcfe6c5ea114543ff473cbbfd7c6f\"><code>892eacd</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/027082950068d6e3897b5422ab6cde3168f7d8b0\"><code>0270829</code></a>\n⚡️ Reduce memory usage in dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16049\">#16049</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/ae031be7b5a2df589f63f4d25389cf07b7b8fc86\"><code>ae031be</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f3644b33cdaf1b14868d77f1c309e0a455c6bac8\"><code>f3644b3</code></a>\n📝 Fix links in docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/15967\">#15967</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1e24ca0e12e9a66cecb1e42780b9116374e2618d\"><code>1e24ca0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/513c396322664bcb3bdcb3946c440a8ed8ef080b\"><code>513c396</code></a>\n👷 Add CI memory benchmark (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16046\">#16046</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/a64dfbbd21a445288ff583d58e1f646fe6baf3af\"><code>a64dfbb</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/4f155486f0c1465c5e1f8701544acc10cb8a78bb\"><code>4f15548</code></a>\n📝 Add Library Skills documentation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16041\">#16041</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/704fbe1439341994100622853f515a8af7ccc2eb\"><code>704fbe1</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.139.2...0.140.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `greenlet` from 3.5.3 to 3.5.4\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/blob/master/CHANGES.rst\">greenlet's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>3.5.4 (2026-07-22)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a crash (segfault) on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14 and\nlater when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet that was\nstarted from a non-empty C-stack-reference state is active.\nSee <code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a potential use-after-free on free-threaded builds of Python 3.14\nand later when the garbage collector runs while a greenlet is\nsuspended holding a <code>_PyCStackRef</code> (for example, mid\nattribute\nresolution). See\n<code>issue 515\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/515&gt;</code>_.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a deadlock on free-threaded builds when a greenlet switch\nhappened\nwhile a <code>PyCriticalSection</code> was held -- for example inside\nasyncio's\n<code>Task.__step</code>, which holds one on the running task for the\nduration of\nthe step. See <code>PR 519\n&lt;https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/pull/519/&gt;</code>.\nThanks to ddorian and Kumar Aditya.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. note::\nBinary 3.15 wheels are now built with Python 3.15b4. These may not\nbe compatible with earlier or later versions of 3.15. Binary\n3.15 wheels of greenlet from previous releases (e.g., 3.5.3)\nmay not be compatible with Python 3.15b4.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/384be8821a934fbb835e369dda2b9b72107e80be\"><code>384be88</code></a>\nPreparing release 3.5.4</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/bbdf57b8cccc572639103005bc7dee41d1c309a2\"><code>bbdf57b</code></a>\nAdd note to CHANGES about versions of 3.15 binary wheels may/not be\ncompatibl...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/759902381a85e2ebca2102fab50ffb99b2227a2b\"><code>7599023</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/517\">#517</a>\nfrom ddorian/issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/73a0a1aadf8d45db71754954d588d433fa826a2a\"><code>73a0a1a</code></a>\nFix the suspended C-stack-ref GC test to catch its regression</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/1ff35f431f768e854db323ae14274044a06d9d12\"><code>1ff35f4</code></a>\nMerge branch 'master' into issue515-c-stack-refs</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/847fb824f6c0590d87963c38c4b2f452a0980b37\"><code>847fb82</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/520\">#520</a>\nfrom dynapx/fix-test-extension-npd</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/0b471ba66bed12fcf7bef969f26705a30a29a5b4\"><code>0b471ba</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/issues/519\">#519</a>\nfrom ddorian/freethread-switch-critical-section</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/d55914df27b30af452e63eb2be41fc9b3ec2c982\"><code>d55914d</code></a>\nSimplify the CHANGES.rst entry</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/78932dc67b6571a920751339cfd88056144e8116\"><code>78932dc</code></a>\nChange notes are for end users, they don't need to go into technical\ndetail</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/commit/39bf70c2cb8c8996ce26bc20e4161fd94c05d380\"><code>39bf70c</code></a>\nHold the C-stack ref snapshot in a std::vector&lt;OwnedObject&gt;</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/python-greenlet/greenlet/compare/3.5.3...3.5.4\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `openai` from 2.46.0 to 2.48.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/releases\">openai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.48.0</h2>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.47.0</h2>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and\nprivate-production-repo support in workflow templates (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/4303e974f08394789c6075b6745357b2f1c36e21\">4303e97</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> require patched aiohttp on Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3515\">#3515</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/d4dceb221b9a92c55c232d5b330ae89beb539415\">d4dceb2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">openai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.48.0 (2026-07-23)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.47.0...v2.48.0\">v2.47.0...v2.48.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> accept <code>None</code> for\nprompt_cache_key/safety_identifier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/36820e69ba6cf1dc3f8d411e48a36e56084fbbc4\">36820e6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add support for <code>spend_limit</code> admin\napis (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1ff13afb6e831394036686a1c352bbec6d704c68\">1ff13af</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.47.0 (2026-07-21)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.46.0...v2.47.0\">v2.46.0...v2.47.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> Add experimental runtime support for HTTPX2\nclients (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3524\">#3524</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/317260cd16395b2338bcdaacd7daa0b179c90105\">317260c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>stlc:</strong> configurable CI runner and p...\n\n_Description has been truncated_\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T10:03:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/79857d462d5ea14c181db33c22bdbdeac477613f/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037"}]},{"sha":"49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ5MjcwYjE3OGMwZjZjYzU1OGI1NTRjMzNkYzQyZTljMjZjYmUwMzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-07-27T08:22:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T08:22:09Z"},"message":"ci(deps): consolidate Dependabot PR surface (#648)\n\nThe open bot-PR list reached **15**. Two structural causes in\n`dependabot.yml`, both fixed here.\n\n## 1. Four `uv` entries → one\n\n`/core-api`, `/core-storage-api`, `/core-worker` and `/core-operations`\nwere four **separate** ecosystem entries, so each emitted its own\n`uv-minor-patch` group PR every week — that's #641, #642, #643, #644\nopen right now, four near-identical PRs.\n\nCollapsed into **one** entry using `directories`, so a run produces a\nsingle grouped PR spanning whichever services actually changed.\n\n## 2. Majors were one-PR-per-dependency\n\n6 of the 15 open PRs are individual majors (structlog 25→26, redis 5→8,\ncroniter 2→6, `setup-python` 5→7, `release-please-action` 4→5, …). Each\necosystem now also has a **`*-majors` group**, so majors are batched\ninto **one reviewable PR** instead of one each.\n\nThey stay **out** of the minor/patch group — a breaking bump is still\nnever smuggled in alongside routine ones; it's just no longer N separate\nPRs.\n\n## Net effect\n\nAt most **two PRs per ecosystem per run** (one minor/patch, one majors),\nwith the four uv services sharing a single PR. Projected: **15 → ~6-7**.\nNothing is auto-merged in this repo — every PR still needs a human\nmerge.\n\n## Known follow-up (not in this PR)\n\n**#640** (`actions/setup-python` 5→7) fails CI with **18 ruff lint\nerrors** (SIM115, C408, …) in `tests/`. That's tool *float*, not a real\nregression from the action bump: this repo installs its lint tooling\nunpinned, so a newer ruff enables new rules and turns PRs red — the same\nfailure class as the fleet-wide ruff 0.16 break (#878).\ncaura-memclaw-enterprise fixed this by installing CI dependencies from\nthe frozen lock (#879 → #890); the equivalent fix here is worth its own\nissue.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7c7aebc391dd1c1560860e30187e95bb9acd853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/b7c7aebc391dd1c1560860e30187e95bb9acd853"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZxUxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGMUQAG4sBuz2T6k1NLE9e8YIqdc8\nSxNaLufRyUaumLU46s7diupTIf0nn5qzH9sq5vBpBwX8SSxa15KsSV4EftFyIXoJ\nvHSCXByuHbiTUyVRD3tuStNK+eViyUFDUL4mwXFCB9X06HMbPdssBr1NB1cBy2D3\ng2tv0ALYajPP6cZFj2Tk8Mk55X/wk1V+vGBGxe6zEmAqexdPICliIQu1GhPffYZQ\nnn0N6TOkNqEMk+m2qupx5Xx8Nghd7tnagN07HJrT1WOZ6H9MBFFJBcXweMvHBdnU\neD5Pa+IKfQD7blnKPUMxPGaJUxNMSpeR/Rqzn43xk1A5/uFtz6XgHddYMjvlfcGu\n8p8vlcYGibMk2/p/P4TH9viTb9qBGfg6Sm1nwpM8NlwG11BIq9FOBejhys5Oz3PQ\n6FK59qV0U0HSUappLh/qKhPRfM/LE9KBqf5sjdxYLTQXUg2VYVCbFxggaYWoU4Ue\nuZJbHOv5Wfop6hNVoDGS321cBtPvjogcEhsyBULT9P8SnWZLtTd3jEZ3/dWEYY8/\ntfoDeo8yWNpmCUargHjp6RYaY6cfwMezYyyfChKaJnoc2x4/wvdwur4xZpaw/zDm\ndLp0hGAvkdYHXqruAqe5P/iK27UZHPJDPJUJqHLzI4TULnaGgy+SNxfRVOOqh1Yv\n6nDrmLfH0LFLC0P+gRDH\n=9JQY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b7c7aebc391dd1c1560860e30187e95bb9acd853\nparent a19bb747051b329001a5fccef24ac30b95b6a20f\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1785140529 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785140529 +0300\n\nci(deps): consolidate Dependabot PR surface (#648)\n\nThe open bot-PR list reached **15**. Two structural causes in\n`dependabot.yml`, both fixed here.\n\n## 1. Four `uv` entries → one\n\n`/core-api`, `/core-storage-api`, `/core-worker` and `/core-operations`\nwere four **separate** ecosystem entries, so each emitted its own\n`uv-minor-patch` group PR every week — that's #641, #642, #643, #644\nopen right now, four near-identical PRs.\n\nCollapsed into **one** entry using `directories`, so a run produces a\nsingle grouped PR spanning whichever services actually changed.\n\n## 2. Majors were one-PR-per-dependency\n\n6 of the 15 open PRs are individual majors (structlog 25→26, redis 5→8,\ncroniter 2→6, `setup-python` 5→7, `release-please-action` 4→5, …). Each\necosystem now also has a **`*-majors` group**, so majors are batched\ninto **one reviewable PR** instead of one each.\n\nThey stay **out** of the minor/patch group — a breaking bump is still\nnever smuggled in alongside routine ones; it's just no longer N separate\nPRs.\n\n## Net effect\n\nAt most **two PRs per ecosystem per run** (one minor/patch, one majors),\nwith the four uv services sharing a single PR. Projected: **15 → ~6-7**.\nNothing is auto-merged in this repo — every PR still needs a human\nmerge.\n\n## Known follow-up (not in this PR)\n\n**#640** (`actions/setup-python` 5→7) fails CI with **18 ruff lint\nerrors** (SIM115, C408, …) in `tests/`. That's tool *float*, not a real\nregression from the action bump: this repo installs its lint tooling\nunpinned, so a newer ruff enables new rules and turns PRs red — the same\nfailure class as the fleet-wide ruff 0.16 break (#878).\ncaura-memclaw-enterprise fixed this by installing CI dependencies from\nthe frozen lock (#879 → #890); the equivalent fix here is worth its own\nissue.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T08:22:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/49270b178c0f6cc558b554c33dc42e9c26cbe037/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followe